t': "Ben that's stirred a couple of thoughts a little longer on the work by affordances because there's this really nice distinction in their work between what they call well, I'm not sure if they I think I think that the term landscape of affordances is a little bit older, but they make this distinction between a landscape of affordances and a field of affordances. And I think the reason this is really important to get on the table is because this distinction is kind of directly targeting the dynamic, shifting, very affective nature of affordances. So on the one hand, you have this landscape of affordances that is relatively static. So right now my landscape of affordances is Brighton. And the landscape of affordances in that sense is not really going to change very rapidly unless I kind of jump on a plane and go somewhere else. But the field of affordances has this thoroughly kind of normative, affective character to it. So depending on my internal state at any given time, depending on my expectations or my desires, say, my field of affordances is going to shift very rapidly. So not just predicated on my internal state, but also kind of contextual cues as well. So if something were to happen in the environment that was afforded very high precision weight in, then that's likely to shift my field of affordances significantly. I think that the reason that I'm kind of emphasizing this to Darius's point is and kind of building on what Mark said, it doesn't seem like this distinction at least would apply from the perspective of the wall, say, because this kind of affectivity and normativity just isn't a feature of the wall's experience of the world. And also to kind of run with affordances. Perhaps you could say a bit more about how you would kind of think about this. Darius because affordances are kind of opportunities for to. There's some debate about this, but I like to think of them as like a relational property between you have the skilled capabilities of an embodied agent and then you have some feature of the environment. So I think when you're thinking from the perspective of the wall, you have the features of the environment because you. Have the embodied characteristics of the agent are kind of playing that role. But it's not clear to me what the kind of skilled capabilities of the wall is. So yeah, if you could just say a bit more about that.", 'words': [{'text': 'Ben', 'start': 1891450, 'end': 1892230, 'confidence': 0.93265, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': "that's", 'start': 1894090, 'end': 1894690, 'confidence': 0.64948, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'stirred', 'start': 1894770, 'end': 1895310, 'confidence': 0.45787, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 1895410, 'end': 1895626, 'confidence': 0.92, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'couple', 'start': 1895648, 'end': 1895786, 'confidence': 0.99586, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'of', 'start': 1895808, 'end': 1895994, 'confidence': 0.61, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'thoughts', 'start': 1896032, 'end': 1896810, 'confidence': 0.63367, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'a', 'start': 1900270, 'end': 1900586, 'confidence': 0.97, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'little', 'start': 1900608, 'end': 1900842, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'longer', 'start': 1900896, 'end': 1901258, 'confidence': 0.99991, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'on', 'start': 1901344, 'end': 1902026, 'confidence': 0.99995, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'the', 'start': 1902208, 'end': 1902554, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'work', 'start': 1902592, 'end': 1902842, 'confidence': 0.99667, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'by', 'start': 1902896, 'end': 1903500, 'confidence': 0.74007, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'affordances', 'start': 1904830, 'end': 1905734, 'confidence': 0.53695, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'because', 'start': 1905782, 'end': 1906042, 'confidence': 0.99991, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': "there's", 'start': 1906096, 'end': 1906326, 'confidence': 0.99873, 'speaker': 'A'}, {'text': 'this', 'start': 1906358, 'end': 1906650