', 'renaissance', 'republicans', 'reykjavik', 'maxwell ramstead', 'robin', 'robin carhart harris', 'ron', 'rules', 'salience', 'scott', "scott's", 'senegal', 'slav', 'socialization', 'states', 'stimuli', 'stochastic', 'strategies', 'structures', 'sumato', 'sussex', 'svamato', 'traits', 'triomphe', 'trump', 'turns', 'tv', 'us', 'universite', 'variational', 'verses', 'waddington', "waddington's", 'wade', 'walter', 'weighting', 'wikipedia', 'wollongong', 'worlds', 'youtube'], 'boost_param': 'low', 'filter_profanity': False, 'redact_pii': False, 'redact_pii_audio': False, 'redact_pii_audio_quality': None, 'redact_pii_policies': None, 'redact_pii_sub': None, 'speaker_labels': True, 'content_safety': False, 'iab_categories': True, 'content_safety_labels': {'status': 'unavailable', 'results': [], 'summary': {}}, 'iab_categories_result': {'status': 'success', 'results': [{'text': "You. All right. July 25, 2023. And we are in the discussion section, basics of Active Inference. This is the first discussion section that we've had for this course, so thank you all for joining. And it's going to be regarding the topics that Ben White introduced in his recent lecture. So everyone will be welcome to pop in and introduce themselves. And then I know that Ben has some ideas to discuss and many other spontaneous and written questions will come into play.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.16882725059986115, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.08033766597509384, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.014753947034478188, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.012167573906481266, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.00856142956763506, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.005801014136523008, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004087027627974749, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.002026983071118593, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001958312001079321, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.001816502190195024, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 420, 'end': 44468}, 'sentences_idx_start': 0, 'sentences_idx_end': 7}, {'text': "So with that exit for now and pass to perhaps some of our first time live streaming guests, I guess I've already spoken, so I may as well continue. So I'm Darius. I am Master's student. I'm just about to finish at UCL in sort of social distributed cognition. I work in a social cognition lab looking at salience regulation and attentional mechanisms within social contexts, but all within an active inference framework, within the Bayesian brain hypothesis framework.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8446367383003235, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.1527072638273239, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.136918306350708, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.030468568205833435, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.02145436592400074, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}, {'relevance': 0.0207088440656662, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.015208170749247074, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.011039825156331062, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00729267718270421, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0045225005596876144, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Dating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 44634, 'end': 94202}, 'sentences_idx_start': 8, 'sentences_idx_end': 12}, {'text': "And, yeah, it's a sort of recent discovery and obsession. And so I'm sort of getting to grips with both the high road and the low road. And so I've had the opportunity to chat to Mark and some other researchers who have been super informative, but always looking to learn more and get my head around even more of the sort of philosophical and mathematical theory. Cool. Sounds good. Hi, everyone. Can you hear me? Yep. I'm Francisco Balsan.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8549103140830994, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.47557830810546875, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.009215358644723892, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0033916619140654802, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0023322117049247026, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0018860140116885304, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0018134561832994223, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0017294043209403753, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0012725433334708214, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0009842545259743929, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 94346, 'end': 129022}, 'sentences_idx_start': 13, 'sentences_idx_end': 21}, {'text': "I'm a PhD student at the University of Bologna, Italy, actually working on intersection between artificial intelligence and education. I have a background in cognitive anthropology and philosophy of science, and I met Axel and Maxlin a few years ago. So I dive into the rabbit hole of active inference and currently pretty much interested in multiscale active inference models of scientific cognition. So pretty interested about the agent level modeling of scientific reasoning assumption that might emerge from the interaction with a scientific environment.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9954391121864319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.2871962785720825, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.09304046630859375, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01759358122944832, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006444504950195551, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.005375253967940807, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.003000571858137846, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002794082975015044, 'label': 'Education>Homeschooling'}, {'relevance': 0.0027265457902103662, 'label': 'Education'}, {'relevance': 0.0026194879319518805, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 129106, 'end': 169842}, 'sentences_idx_start': 22, 'sentences_idx_end': 25}, {'text': "So we're referring to scientific nature, construction and all these type of top down and bottom up interactions. So super interested to hear something from you. Thank you. Thank you very much. Would anybody else like to introduce themselves before we start? So you go first. Okay. Hi, I'm Regina Sagin. You can call me Gina. I'm from Guatemala. And well, I'm not from the social sciences. I come from biology and neuroscience.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9991518259048462, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.026405591517686844, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.014703059569001198, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.010433579795062542, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.00949062965810299, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.008217547088861465, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.00768946623429656, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.006244969088584185, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.005537934601306915, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005370973143726587, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 169906, 'end': 207828}, 'sentences_idx_start': 26, 'sentences_idx_end': 37}, {'text': "And I'm here because I'm working on a project as a technical operator in this big project in the Xscape and material minds. And I do the technical part and experiments, but I want to learn the philosophical part. That's the background that makes the theory of everything. We're going to experiment. So I'm here to learn.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12578748166561127, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.12380694597959518, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.04711611941456795, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.02620747685432434, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.011942824348807335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.005290823522955179, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.003905758261680603, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003218571888282895, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0024605714716017246, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015598536701872945, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 207924, 'end': 233330}, 'sentences_idx_start': 38, 'sentences_idx_end': 42}, {'text': "And also, I am like when you see the Olympics, that you see all the swimmers, and I wish there was a normal guy to see how good these people are so you could compare. So that's me today, right? I understand half of what's going on, but I'm happy to be here, so yeah. Hi. Sorry. I'm Leigh. So my name is Lee. I'm a PhD student at the University of York studying systems transformation.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.10099882632493973, 'label': 'Sports>Swimming'}, {'relevance': 0.015784110873937607, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.010766792111098766, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>SportingEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.010315882042050362, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.006680860184133053, 'label': 'Sports>TrackAndField'}, {'relevance': 0.004672712180763483, 'label': 'Sports'}, {'relevance': 0.003939274698495865, 'label': 'Sports>OlympicSports>SummerOlympicSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0034211785532534122, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0033680207561701536, 'label': 'Sports>DisabledSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0033479181583970785, 'label': 'Sports>OlympicSports'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 234340, 'end': 270120}, 'sentences_idx_start': 43, 'sentences_idx_end': 50}, {'text': "And I'm joining because I'm using perceptual control theory at the minute to model examples of effective practice in organizations. And I've read quite a lot of active inference papers, and I understand that there's a lot of resonance overlap between perceptual control theory and active inference, although I understand it's within a predictive framework.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9913414120674133, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.546090841293335, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.015150893479585648, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.009677991271018982, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ManagementConsultingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.006301551125943661, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0036084894090890884, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0022376656997948885, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessAdministration'}, {'relevance': 0.0016650027828291059, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.001425480586476624, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0012487320927903056, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 271420, 'end': 299404}, 'sentences_idx_start': 51, 'sentences_idx_end': 52}, {'text': "And also it's kind of a level of abstraction higher, so you're able to kind of quantify the difference between sort of the predictive state or the outcome state and the current state. So what I'm really trying to understand is how might that level of abstraction be useful in what I'm doing, actually, because I understand it's a much more kind of concurrent theory and framework than perceptual control theory. Yeah, very cool. Anybody else? Is that everybody?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.051346004009246826, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01379816047847271, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0042751505970954895, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.003496206132695079, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.003487883135676384, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.002882106928154826, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002047910587862134, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0019156812923029065, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0011929537868127227, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0011281047482043505, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 299532, 'end': 338980}, 'sentences_idx_start': 53, 'sentences_idx_end': 57}, {'text': "Okay, well, has everybody seen the lecture that I gave a couple of weeks ago? Okay, so I think it might be helpful then, if I kind of very briefly go over what we covered in that lecture just to kind of jog people's memories, and then we can maybe pick up some questions from there. So the lecture last week was on the basics of active inference, and it was intended to be an introduction to the framework on a very abstract, philosophical level.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.053751345723867416, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00987242255359888, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.007603490725159645, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0035863006487488747, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0019222567789256573, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0015439654234796762, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.00139777606818825, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.001251650508493185, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0012353331549093127, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.001046567689627409, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 341670, 'end': 373374}, 'sentences_idx_start': 58, 'sentences_idx_end': 60}, {'text': "So it left out all of the kind of mathematics and technical aspects of the framework. And the objective really was to lay the groundwork for future weeks in this course, because this is obviously a course on active inference in the social sciences. And so in the subsequent weeks, we're going to be looking at topics like collective behavior, social cognition, shared norms, and niche construction.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8540799021720886, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.8002210855484009, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.1856578290462494, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.02167639136314392, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.010407768189907074, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.009485646151006222, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0029516038484871387, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MediaIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00276733236387372, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.0018879843410104513, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0015252053271979094, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 373412, 'end': 398914}, 'sentences_idx_start': 61, 'sentences_idx_end': 63}, {'text': 'And so what I wanted to do was to put on the table a kind of fully fleshed out picture of what the individual agent looks like in active inference. And so to do this, we looked at emotion, agency, mind, so we looked at kind of the role of action and perception, the role of internal representations in active inference.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.18485145270824432, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007406634744256735, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.006872966885566711, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.004842924419790506, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004658964928239584, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.001651869504712522, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.001490654656663537, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0013281501596793532, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010388531954959035, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0010155050549656153, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 399042, 'end': 427066}, 'sentences_idx_start': 64, 'sentences_idx_end': 65}, {'text': "And then as a case study, we looked at an active inference based account of addiction to kind of bring all of these threads together, to kind of articulate a lot of the things that I'd said in the previous sections. The questions here don't have to be specifically tethered to that lecture.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.998462438583374, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SubstanceAbuse'}, {'relevance': 0.005387681070715189, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>SmokingCessation'}, {'relevance': 0.0053731948137283325, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0018763479311019182, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}, {'relevance': 0.001107840216718614, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>PharmaceuticalDrugs'}, {'relevance': 0.0010258392430841923, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Crime'}, {'relevance': 0.0009931797394528985, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0007206446607597172, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityScandal'}, {'relevance': 0.0006634121527895331, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.0004099536163266748, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>Casinos&Gambling'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 427178, 'end': 450786}, 'sentences_idx_start': 66, 'sentences_idx_end': 67}, {'text': "I suppose we can just start with any general questions about active inference and philosophy and how active inference applies to individual agents, or if anybody did want to pick up on any threads from the lecture, then we can go from there. Can I ask something just for the basic questions? Yeah, of course. I don't understand because I think you explain it later, but how does creativity and science in general enters active imperents?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6769465804100037, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.03699414059519768, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.006185449659824371, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0032013985328376293, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0025219435337930918, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002164713107049465, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015936974668875337, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0015614124713465571, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013039266923442483, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0010077005717903376, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 450898, 'end': 482770}, 'sentences_idx_start': 68, 'sentences_idx_end': 71}, {'text': "How does trying to be creative and not doing what you predict enters this room? Yeah, this is a really good question. Did you see the lecture? Yeah, but I remember half of it. That's fine, but do you remember the dark room problem? Yeah, I know that's where the answer is. I think there are several interesting dark room problem, some of them more interesting than others.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03268370032310486, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.008706453256309032, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.008072171360254288, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0069082919508218765, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.006532412953674793, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.005670822225511074, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.005104518961161375, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004554165527224541, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.00445881113409996, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.002949927467852831, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 483130, 'end': 521410}, 'sentences_idx_start': 72, 'sentences_idx_end': 78}, {'text': "And I tried to cover I obviously didn't have time to cover all of those in the lecture. But for those that perhaps aren't familiar, the dark room problem is this kind of canonical philosophical worry about predictive processing and active inference that says essentially, if all we're trying to do is minimize prediction errors, why don't we just find maximally predictable environments? And why do we not just lay in a dark room hooked up to an intravenous drip and enjoy kind of error free lifestyle?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06704144179821014, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005164240952581167, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0024897167459130287, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0022728408221155405, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002265953691676259, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.002227965509518981, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.001888065249659121, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0010048249969258904, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006937138387002051, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0004506670229602605, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 521480, 'end': 556250}, 'sentences_idx_start': 79, 'sentences_idx_end': 81}, {'text': "So I think that's the question that you're articulating there. I just quickly see a hand from Darius. Darius, did you want to jump in, or was it a separate question? It's a separate question. So I thought I would just do it in advance. But yeah, no, ignore me. I'll circle a call background in a second then. But feel free, I should say.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.46282240748405457, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>HomeUtilities>PhoneServices'}, {'relevance': 0.03711393475532532, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.0021357364021241665, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TelecommunicationsIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0010697997640818357, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>AudioProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0010095734614878893, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.0005343490047380328, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>Smartphones'}, {'relevance': 0.0004834336577914655, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries>FirstAid'}, {'relevance': 0.0004395698197185993, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>VideoProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.00040328429895453155, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0002720983175095171, 'label': 'Sports>Golf'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 556910, 'end': 575506}, 'sentences_idx_start': 82, 'sentences_idx_end': 89}, {'text': "Actually, this is the first time I've kind of chaired a discussion like this, so I'll be explicit and say people should just feel free to jump in whenever they want. If you want to take the disco, if you want to kind of add something or kind of build on a question that we're answering, feel free to jump in.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.12652720510959625, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>Concerts&MusicEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.054067354649305344, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>Nightclubs'}, {'relevance': 0.026288850232958794, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.014910460449755192, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.007685996126383543, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.006706527434289455, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PersonalCelebrations&LifeEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.005798022728413343, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>BusinessExpos&Conferences'}, {'relevance': 0.004829455632716417, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>TalkRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.004018002655357122, 'label': 'Television>RealityTV'}, {'relevance': 0.003992875572293997, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PersonalCelebrations&LifeEvents>BachelorParty'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 575528, 'end': 591880}, 'sentences_idx_start': 90, 'sentences_idx_end': 91}, {'text': "But, yeah, with the dark room problem, as I'm aware, the first answer to that question and this is something that I did cover in the lecture, is essentially a big part of active inference is to recognize that agents are it's a kind of fundamentally embodied framework, okay? So that can be kind of cashed out in various ways.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9323108792304993, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.012640407308936119, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003536608535796404, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0019703495781868696, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0016182977706193924, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0010556700872257352, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0010521083604544401, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0007217343081720173, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.0007100441143848002, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0006498224101960659, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 592970, 'end': 614462}, 'sentences_idx_start': 92, 'sentences_idx_end': 93}, {'text': "But one of the most important ways is that the expected states of the organism or that the agent are necessarily rooted in the phenotype of the organism and the kind of evolutionary biological needs that come with having a particular body. So there was a paper that I referenced in a lecture by there's three authors on this paper. It's andy Clark, Karl Friston, and then I'm forgetting the name of the third author. If anybody can recall, feel free to drop it in the chat.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9715814590454102, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.8648644089698792, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0321221724152565, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004724087659269571, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0045467158779501915, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.002266688970848918, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0009730490855872631, 'label': 'Pets>Reptiles'}, {'relevance': 0.0009352592169307172, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.0008425712585449219, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0007895992021076381, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PersonalCelebrations&LifeEvents>Birth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 614516, 'end': 645494}, 'sentences_idx_start': 94, 'sentences_idx_end': 97}, {'text': 'But this is an answer to the dark room, where it builds on that notion of embodiment and says, look, creatures like us, human agents, could sit in the dark room and do nothing and just kind of enjoy the very predictable march of hunger, thirst, et cetera. But obviously, those particular biologists out of the room. And so you have this very fundamental level. We have this very fundamental kind of basis upon which we have these needs that need to be met.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05421936884522438, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.022412946447730064, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.009505338035523891, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}, {'relevance': 0.009318429045379162, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.008924996480345726, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}, {'relevance': 0.008800745941698551, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00785757601261139, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.006890163291245699, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>WeightLoss'}, {'relevance': 0.0049478402361273766, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0046980311162769794, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 645622, 'end': 679314}, 'sentences_idx_start': 98, 'sentences_idx_end': 101}, {'text': "And so we need to engage in exploratory behaviors on the topic of novelty, because that's a kind of base. I take that to be a kind of baseline answer. But there are clearly kinds of activities and behaviors that we do engage in going beyond the dark room kind of curiosity play, creativity, engaging in kind of why do we create works of art?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9908804893493652, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.7052295804023743, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.5821456909179688, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.2728933095932007, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.05427723750472069, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.039560459554195404, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts'}, {'relevance': 0.019199708476662636, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.017708515748381615, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.00955813005566597, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.00932279322296381, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 679352, 'end': 706230}, 'sentences_idx_start': 102, 'sentences_idx_end': 104}, {'text': "And there's not an obvious link between those kinds of behaviors and the kinds of biological needs that are emphasized in the original answer to the dark room worry. So in answer to Regina's question about creativity, I think that a good starting point for this is the section on aerodynamics that I introduced in the lecture. So this was the idea that there's this strong connection between affectivity as a kind of emotional, embodied feeling state and the changes to the rate in prediction error minimization.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.24949723482131958, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.042786531150341034, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.04247491434216499, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01949286088347435, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.016775358468294144, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.015357572585344315, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.014771445654332638, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.013050414621829987, 'label':