or is the answer to the puzzle of play.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8755204081535339, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.7960463166236877, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.5468037128448486, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.19747167825698853, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.16524432599544525, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.11718947440385818, 'label': "Shopping>Children'sGamesAndToys"}, {'relevance': 0.006886323913931847, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.005286286119371653, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004965757019817829, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>CasualGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004851479083299637, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>ExerciseAndFitnessVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 773110, 'end': 812382}, 'sentences_idx_start': 113, 'sentences_idx_end': 114}, {'text': "So the puzzle of play is why do we engage in metabolically quite costly and they don't have any obvious benefit. And the idea there is that, well, there's kind of several ideas in there, but one of them is that it just literally feels good because minimizing prediction error feels good to us. So whenever we do better than expect at minimizing prediction error, it feels good.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6839144825935364, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>ExerciseAndFitnessVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.3426523506641388, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.2834438681602478, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.015668297186493874, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.009951900690793991, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00