r kind prediction error minimizing system, we have a really deep temporal model. We're managing uncertainty at a big horizon, maybe even multigenerational, where we're thinking about our kids or our kids.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0065463837236166, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0033431195188313723, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.001029867329634726, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0010101040825247765, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0007074963068589568, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0004592562036123127, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0003861559962388128, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003751550684683025, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.00026658305432647467, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.00026122218696400523, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 871510, 'end': 906310}, 'sentences_idx_start': 121, 'sentences_idx_end': 124}, {'text': "I mean, who knows how deep the Generative model actually runs? It turns out that error over that stops developing error minimizing skills and abilities and just hangs out in one microniche, because that microniche is going to be upset sooner, right? I mean, it's such a great example of where we thought we were in a really set vector state and then suddenly it gets jostled and all of us go, oh my goodness, what do we do? We've been bumped.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.031936753541231155, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.015653161332011223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0044828676618635654, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003297856543213129, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0032753103878349066, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Comput