: 1099800}, 'sentences_idx_start': 153, 'sentences_idx_end': 156}, {'text': "So in the chat I just dropped a link to yeah, so somebody just asked about papers related to hanging out at Edge of Our Capabilities. I'll do that right now. There sure are some papers on that. Mark's got a few.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13970163464546204, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.07046253979206085, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.011844075284898281, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.010665575042366982, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}, {'relevance': 0.007187667302787304, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}, {'relevance': 0.0035579840186983347, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.003011344000697136, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.002914326498284936, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0023394834715873003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0014790742425248027, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1101390, 'end': 1115598}, 'sentences_idx_start': 157, 'sentences_idx_end': 160}, {'text': "I already dropped a link in there to an Aon article by some of the old Expect project crew, including Mark Kate Nave, George Dean and Andy Clark on the value of uncertainty, which is I think it's a really good start point for some of these questions. Just because Aeon is a kind of non academic place where, you know, it's a non technical introduction. And there's a wonderful example in that paper of a guy named I think it's Max Hawkings. Is that right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.026086555793881416, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.002268871758133173, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.002123733051121235, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0016782735474407673, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0011444527190178633, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0011046044528484344, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.001037615817040205, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>RetirementPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.000947214663028717, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.0006992558483034372, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>MutualFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0006972060073167086, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1115684, 'end': 1146474}, 'sentences_idx_start': 161, 'sentences_idx_end': 164}, {'text': "Mark? Max who? He's a kind of tech guy and he realized he was getting kind of bored with his life. He'd inadvertently trapped himself in a dark room because his life had become so rote and scheduled and systematic. He realized that he would be kind of incredibly easy to kidnap because he was in the same place at the same time every single day and he took drastic action to break out of that dark room.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02424178086221218, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Crime'}, {'relevance': 0.006463967263698578, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0037361299619078636, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityScandal'}, {'relevance': 0.003432688768953085, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.00256190518848598, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.002510873368009925, 'label': 'Movies>DramaMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.0019361407030373812, 'label': 'Movies>CrimeAndMysteryMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.0017032703617587686, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00158003403339535, 'label': 'Television>RealityTV'}, {'relevance': 0.001491091912612319, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Fiction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1146512, 'end': 1172722}, 'sentences_idx_start': 165, 'sentences_idx_end': 169}, {'text': "So he kind of introduced a randomization algorithm that it would kind of choose for him where he was going to eat, where he was going to go, which shows he was going to attend. And this example is a really nice centerpiece in this article. I think this is a nice place to start because it's also grounded in discussions about epistemic actions as well, because there's also as cool as play and art and creativity are there's also really good reasons that uncertainty is valuable as well? Right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6456303000450134, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.00629453593865037, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.004204576835036278, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.004035299643874168, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0034422380849719048, 'label': 'Careers>JobSearch'}, {'relevance': 0.003280091332271695, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002763903932645917, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.002625896595418453, 'label': 'Sports>FantasySports'}, {'relevance': 0.0024972124956548214, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.002446905244141817, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1172776, 'end': 1204522}, 'sentences_idx_start': 170, 'sentences_idx_end': 173}, {'text': "Because while we might want to exploit all of the opportunities for kind of nourishment and valuable prediction error minimization in our environment, there are of course going to be times where those opportunities are exhausted and we need to go and explore different ones. And I think there's some stuff in there as well on epistemic actions within the context of navigation as well. So sometimes we're going to have to temporarily move further away from our target in order to minimize our uncertainty about where we're going.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07377694547176361, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0324607789516449, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.008891746401786804, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.005094551481306553, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.002813466126099229, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.002165532438084483, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0021512052044272423, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0021045932080596685, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations'}, {'relevance': 0.002004161011427641, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0016127250855788589, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1204576, 'end': 1239014}, 'sentences_idx_start': 174, 'sentences_idx_end': 176}, {'text': "So there's lots and lots of stuff on the value of uncertainty and it kind of is very much at the forefront of some of the really interesting philosophical applications of the framework. For sure. Okay, by all means. Yeah, we've got time. I know you have a question that is but with the value of uncertainty.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.010650139302015305, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.009292028844356537, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.005608847364783287, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0033692519646137953, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0020797490142285824, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0017436292255297303, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0015857825055718422, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0015612392453476787, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.001514528295956552, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0012346566654741764, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1239132, 'end': 1260442}, 'sentences_idx_start': 177, 'sentences_idx_end': 181}, {'text': "It's just that I'm thinking because I've been working a lot with the magicians and there's a way of using uncertainty as entertainment that it's very difficult to understand as a concept for entertainment. Why would you like to be in a place where you want to predict but you cannot, and you still want to participate in this activity? So for me, magic shows, it's kind of breaking a little.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9989387392997742, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.08850273489952087, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.02934408374130726, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.005262554157525301, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0024849323090165854, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.002065744251012802, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0017461128300055861, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0016877457965165377, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Comedy(MusicAndAudio)'}, {'relevance': 0.0012537928996607661, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0008127064793370664, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>CardGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1260506, 'end': 1287320}, 'sentences_idx_start': 182, 'sentences_idx_end': 184}, {'text': "Spoke to I forget the person's name, but there was an Xcape meeting here at Sussex and I spoke to one of the guys on Escape who had been working on magic. I don't know if you know who I'm talking about, but I think they have a book on magic. And I think that's really cool to think about from a predictive processing perspective, the idea that magic is just these wonderful kind of violations of expectations.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9981765747070312, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.005628906190395355, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00042091772775165737, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.00035059565561823547, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0002906428708229214, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002529230550862849, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00022902971250005066, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>ComputerAnimation'}, {'relevance': 0.00022831287060398608, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>CardGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0001901497016660869, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.00014786947576794773, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1290730, 'end': 1314410}, 'sentences_idx_start': 185, 'sentences_idx_end': 187}, {'text': "In a certain sense, I think predictive processing provides a nice, really intuitive framework for thinking about those kinds of things. One little point there, Regina. Just about again, if it feels paradoxical just to sort of complexify your view, remember that this is always happening in a hierarchical system. So just because you have errors at one level of the system doesn't mean you're going to have sort of critical, cascading, unbearable errors at higher levels.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.2346222847700119, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0317685529589653, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0131255267187953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.003092588158324361, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002526695840060711, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0016794707626104355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0013557603815570474, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.001022494863718748, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0009182670619338751, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0006610717973671854, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1314570, 'end': 1342802}, 'sentences_idx_start': 188, 'sentences_idx_end': 191}, {'text': "So that's why it's fun to go to horror movies. So I dropped the paper here. Also, we have a new paper coming out on horror movies. I'm pretty interested in this, but it's the same as going to the magic show in some way. Now, the reason why those errors are fun is because we're safe in a theater. We're with our friends. We have lots of sugar in our system from eating popcorn and candy.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9821045994758606, 'label': 'Movies>HorrorMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.1568477898836136, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>CinemasAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.1302454024553299, 'label': 'Movies>IndieAndArthouseMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.11211608350276947, 'label': 'Movies'}, {'relevance': 0.09217963367700577, 'label': 'Movies>ComedyMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.014682048000395298, 'label': 'Movies>CrimeAndMysteryMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.011891987174749374, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeEntertaining'}, {'relevance': 0.011810794472694397, 'label': 'Movies>FantasyMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.007227291353046894, 'label': 'Movies>DramaMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.005306667648255825, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1342946, 'end': 1366910}, 'sentences_idx_start': 192, 'sentences_idx_end': 198}, {'text': "We can control the amount of scary by covering our eyes. There's lots of control here. And yet we're getting media that's pinging all of our evolutionarily ancient error tracking systems so that we're getting jumps in the physiology as if there's a bunch of volatility that we need to manage, and yet we're in a completely safe space, which is really fun for our kind of system because we're hierarchically deep predictive systems. The high level here isn't jeopardized.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.96831214427948, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.10996191203594208, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.08888986706733704, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.017278851941227913, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.016863901168107986, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006389813032001257, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.006278452463448048, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.005263662431389093, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004550202749669552, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.003672105958685279, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1367490, 'end': 1397798}, 'sentences_idx_start': 199, 'sentences_idx_end': 202}, {'text': "It knows I'm in a theater, but the low level stuff is still registering all sorts of literal volatilities. But of course, they get squashed. They don't cascade all the way up. Or if you're the kind of person where they do tend to cascade all the way up, then you're also the kind of person who doesn't like going to horror movies because it kind of scares you.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7041375041007996, 'label': 'Movies>HorrorMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.49700161814689636, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>CinemasAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.026964157819747925, 'label': 'Movies>IndieAndArthouseMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.022360162809491158, 'label': 'Movies'}, {'relevance': 0.009597189724445343, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeEntertaining'}, {'relevance': 0.0039624846540391445, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.0017748558893799782, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>HomeEntertainmentSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.001658608322031796, 'label': 'Movies>DocumentaryMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.0013887024251744151, 'label': 'Movies>FantasyMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.001256345771253109, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1397974, 'end': 1418286}, 'sentences_idx_start': 203, 'sentences_idx_end': 206}, {'text': "Go home and think, oh, goodness, maybe ghosts are real and maybe I live with them. You wouldn't be going there then. So with magic, it's the same sort of thing with error. I don't know if you've ever who does the really extreme magic. David Blaine, where he was in a block. Yeah, david Blaine, have you ever seen him?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9629297852516174, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.9029834866523743, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.000855888007208705, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0004856247396674007, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0003028382488992065, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00022413305123336613, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>Photography'}, {'relevance': 0.00019181592506356537, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>CardGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00015225382230710238, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0001506422267993912, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0001424641814082861, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1418388, 'end': 1445318}, 'sentences_idx_start': 207, 'sentences_idx_end': 212}, {'text': "He goes to Haiti where you have a community that really believes in magic, and he does some magic and he gets into trouble. Like suddenly all the young men are, no, no, that's no bueno. That you're doing this. And then the camera pans back and he, no, no, hold you here, I'll show you how it's done. It was just a trick. I'll just show you outside.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9910591244697571, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.0005166513728909194, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.00046976684825494885, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.00021749359439127147, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0002138222916983068, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>ComputerAnimation'}, {'relevance': 0.00019331509247422218, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>SouthAmericaTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.00018694164464250207, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries'}, {'relevance': 0.000185281372978352, 'label': 'FineArt>Dance'}, {'relevance': 0.00017965657752938569, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}, {'relevance': 0.00015861277643125504, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1445324, 'end': 1462494}, 'sentences_idx_start': 213, 'sentences_idx_end': 218}, {'text': "It's not real magic because there they're not having fun with it anymore. They're like, no, that's not a good thing to do. So it just goes to show that our engagement with magic is mostly a sort of scary play, I think. One thing I just kind of sorry about the seagulls. I don't know if you can hear those. There are seagulls going crazy just outside my window.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9979718327522278, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.010688260197639465, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0005862534162588418, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>CardGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0005654470296576619, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.0002627278445288539, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00024392236082348973, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries'}, {'relevance': 0.00021030937205068767, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.00017708436644170433, 'label': 'Shopping>LotteriesAndScratchcards'}, {'relevance': 0.0001561813405714929, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>TheaterVenuesAndEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.00015235402679536492, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1462532, 'end': 1486710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 219, 'sentences_idx_end': 224}, {'text': "One thing I would add is, I think, another aspect to this part of the framework wherein you have this value of prediction error, kind of epistemic and effective emotional value of prediction error. It's one of the kind of key elements in this notion of agency get in active inference that I think is really going to be really important to in mind as you go through the further weeks of this course.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.022712193429470062, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.009877714328467846, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.008422493934631348, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.005917096044868231, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003174923127517104, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003062259405851364, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0022283599246293306, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.001961980713531375, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0016919835470616817, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0013030711561441422, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1487450, 'end': 1513902}, 'sentences_idx_start': 225, 'sentences_idx_end': 226}, {'text': "As well, like I said in the lecture, it's not necessarily speaking to the metaphysical question of free will, but it's certainly moving us away from this picture of the agent as a kind of automaton that's just following rules. There's real space here for kind of individuality and creativity as well. Okay, Darius has been waiting a little while, so let's go over to him. Happily patient, happily mean.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.815227746963501, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.02353936806321144, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.010139433667063713, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.00806343276053667, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.007967325858771801, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.004622935317456722, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.004407733213156462, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.002531148726120591, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0023581343702971935, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0019838307052850723, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1513956, 'end': 1543846}, 'sentences_idx_start': 227, 'sentences_idx_end': 230}, {'text': "This is this question, I guess, is deriving from my thoughts about the meeting of the high road and the low road, some of the recent work that's been coming out of Maxwell Ramstead and actually a conversation I had with him, which is that the generative model.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.18025602400302887, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007239244878292084, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.005727234296500683, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004826937802135944, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003960678353905678, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002870002528652549, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}, {'relevance': 0.0010363117326050997, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0010111164301633835, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0009284003172069788, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008673010161146522, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1543868, 'end': 1559420}, 'sentences_idx_start': 231, 'sentences_idx_end': 231}, {'text': "So my question, given that given and talk is regarding the notion of affordances, I think it's natural that as cognitive scientists and philosophers, we take the perspective intuitively of the agent in the agent arena relationship and how the agent is in the business of reducing prediction error. I was just wondering whether, as philosophers, you and Mark have thought about what is it like for the whole system to be in the business of reducing its prediction error? So I'm interested in flow states.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03264632821083069, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.029555348679423332, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.02002427913248539, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.014227962121367455, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.012996871024370193, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.003743894165381789, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.003363266820088029, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.0029468529392033815, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0029413942247629166, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0024713485036045313, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1562450, 'end': 1598578}, 'sentences_idx_start': 232, 'sentences_idx_end': 234}, {'text': "And so, for example, my thinking is that in a canonical example of a flow state, let's say a rock climber, the climbing wall, is also in the business of reducing its prediction error as to afford the opportunity for it to be exploited stealth or themselves are in the business of reducing prediction error. So I'm wondering whether this expansion of affordances is bi directional trial, infinitely directional, better? That's an amazing question. You mentioned Axel constant, but somebody else. Someone else.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8222652077674866, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.0013284796150401235, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0005366240511648357, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.0003858457785099745, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00029951552278362215, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0002368449349887669, 'label': 'Sports>Skiing'}, {'relevance': 0.00023469234292861074, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.00022773868113290519, 'label': 'Sports>AutoRacing>MotorcycleSports'}, {'relevance': 0.00022651208564639091, 'label': 'Education>SpecialEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.00019644471467472613, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>CivilEngineeringIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1598764, 'end': 1642646}, 'sentences_idx_start': 235, 'sentences_idx_end': 239}, {'text': "But I spoke to Maxwell Ramsey's last week. There's a paper on I'll find it in a second. On niche construction and affordances. I think it's Axel comps. They talk about the kind of the symmetry between a niche and an agent. Very much in the same vein as you were just talking about. There this idea that there's not just this unidirectional kind of fit between the agent and the environment or the niche is actually modeling generative model of the agent as well, implicitly.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8830211162567139, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.7910573482513428, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.5060377717018127, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.06737235933542252, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.04028112813830376, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RetailIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.011246893554925919, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.005674630869179964, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GovernmentBusiness'}, {'relevance': 0.0038954606279730797, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.003607387188822031, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.002722113858908415, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1642668, 'end': 1685510}, 'sentences_idx_start': 240, 'sentences_idx_end': 246}, {'text': "So I think the best I can do there direction of some really interesting work on that, but certainly it's not something that plays a central role in my thinking recently. Yeah. So we have the participants chat. Yeah. A variation approach to niche construction. Yeah. I don't know if Mark has anything to add or anybody else worth thinking about. Yeah. Darius, can I just check one thing? You asked.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5894160270690918, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.4351285398006439, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.4260574281215668, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ConstructionIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.02586093544960022, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.016719309613108635, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeImprovement'}, {'relevance': 0.009961029514670372, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.007238871417939663, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RealEstateIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.006670627277344465, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GovernmentBusiness'}, {'relevance': 0.003749196184799075, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.0027082052547484636, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>HousingMarket'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1686250, 'end': 1717822}, 'sentences_idx_start': 247, 'sentences_idx_end': 256}, {'text': "I don't know how much I need to add here, but did you think that the wall was reducing free energy relative to the climber? Did you say that? That's right. I don't know how that can that be the case? Can that be the case? The wall as a thing is maintaining itself relative self evidencing. Right? Yeah. But it's not really a duet of one here.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9846699237823486, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003930126258637756, 'label': 'Sports>Gymnastics'}, {'relevance': 0.0002474873617757112, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.00017801787180360407, 'label': 'Sports>Skiing'}, {'relevance': 0.00016183272236958146, 'label': 'Sports>FigureSkating'}, {'relevance': 0.000125140359159559, 'label': 'RealEstate>LandAndFarms'}, {'relevance': 0.00011116683890577406, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.0001075797263183631, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.00010022176138591021, 'label': 'Sports>AutoRacing>MotorcycleSports'}, {'relevance': 8.378876373171806e-05, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1717876, 'end': 1742454}, 'sentences_idx_start': 257, 'sentences_idx_end': 265}, {'text': "It's not like it has a generative model that's deep, where it's modeling the climber, modeling it the same way as tango dancers do. A tango duo are having cooperative flow states because each movement opens a vista of possible error, minimizing opportunities for the partner, who in turn opens a vista of error minimizing opportunities for the partner and backwards and forwards into this ever opening expanse of affordance capabilities. But an inanimate object and an agent don't really have that same dynamic.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.14384551346302032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.07658696174621582, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.031377553939819336, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.009489226154983044, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.004615472164005041, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004548496566712856, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0038502446841448545, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}, {'relevance': 0.002970145782455802, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>ComputerAnimation'}, {'relevance': 0.002853257115930319, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0009330315515398979, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1742492, 'end': 1774926}, 'sentences_idx_start': 266, 'sentences_idx_end': 268}, {'text': "So I was wondering what you were thinking there. So my thinking was that this kind of bleeds into the notion of fluidity of affordances in the kind of Gibsonian sense and the fluidity of concepts. So I agree in the sense of physical self evidencing, it needs to model the rain, it needs to model the physical environment so as to maintain itself. But what about as it's a for it's it's so a sheer rock face is not a climbing wall.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9938655495643616, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.004727866500616074, 'label': 'Science>Geology'}, {'relevance': 0.002556971274316311, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.0010309593053534627, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0007107729907147586, 'label': 'Sports>Skiing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006179111078381538, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0005326883983798325, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0004508647252805531, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0004424619546625763, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Off-RoadVehicles'}, {'relevance': 0.0004132989561185241, 'label': 'Sports>SportsEquipment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1774958, 'end': 1807498}, 'sentences_idx_start': 269, 'sentences_idx_end': 272}, {'text': "And that's because it doesn't self evidence as a climbing wall, it doesn't offer the affordances to be climbed. That's why I was kind of referring to which is that affordances change based on the agent arena relationship, right. Your car's affordances change whether it's working or broken down. Similarly, the climbing wall changes whether it's got footholds handholds or whether it's just a sheer rock face. That was my thinking.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9326891303062439, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.00066560716368258, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0005536162643693388, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.0005293854046612978, 'label': 'Sports>Skiing'}, {'relevance': 0.00036616012221202254, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.00032397962058894336, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.0003092819533776492, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>LuxuryCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00028646737337112427, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00026771012926474214, 'label': 'RealEstate>RealEstateBuyingAndSelling'}, {'relevance': 0.0002663661143742502, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1807584, 'end': 1826740}, 'sentences_idx_start': 273, 'sentences_idx_end': 277}, {'text': "It seems slightly spooky to me that we'd think of the wall as self evidencing in that way. I think the language that we tend to use because Julian Kirsten, Eric Reitfeld, Yelly Brunberg and folks often use the idea of affordances and fields of affordances in the active inference way.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3933712840080261, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.03380000591278076, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.014368749223649502, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.010853428393602371, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005711515434086323, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0032419716008007526, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.002882446860894561, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.002708496293053031, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.002410714980214834, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0022666275035589933, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1827590, 'end': 1844600}, 'sentences_idx_start': 278, 'sentences_idx_end': 279}, {'text': "The radical end of the pool there is typically that the affordances don't only happen on the agent side, but rather happen from a dynamic of the changing volatile environment and the generative model of the agent and that they're collaborating in dynamic ongoing ways such that the affordances are emergent between them. That certainly seems right to me. The idea to push it a little bit further and think about the wall self evidencing, I think it's a step too spooky for me.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04467596486210823, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.04340192303061485, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>MergersAndAcquisitions'}, {'relevance': 0.03800230473279953, 'label': 'RealEstate>RealEstateBuyingAndSelling'}, {'relevance': 0.02000671811401844, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.01379374973475933, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.01010378822684288, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}, {'relevance': 0.006874467246234417, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.006330220494419336, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00421286653727293, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessUtilities'}, {'relevance': 0.0038340860046446323, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetForBeginners'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1846250, 'end': 1875300}, 'sentences_idx_start': 280, 'sentences_idx_end': 282}, {'text': "I think I would feel safer a little bit closer to thinking about the affordances are changing relative to the dynamics of the wall, but I don't know what it would mean for the wall to be evidencing, the climber or itself.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9922103881835938, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports>Climbing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002867534349206835, 'label': 'Sports>Skiing'}, {'relevance': 0.00023341765336226672, 'label': 'Sports>Gymnastics'}, {'relevance': 0.00019668854656629264, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.00018813311180565506, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0001307502097915858, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.00011995652312180027, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.000119393014756497, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00011540362174855545, 'label': 'RealEstate>LandAndFarms'}, {'relevance': 0.00010570399172138423, 'label': 'Sports>FigureSkating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1875750, 'end': 1891000}, 'sentences_idx_start': 283, 'sentences_idx_end': 283}, {'text': "Ben that's stirred a couple of thoughts a little longer on the work by affordances because there's this really nice distinction in their work between what they call well, I'm not sure if they I think I think that the term landscape of affordances is a little bit older, but they make this distinction between a landscape of affordances and a field of affordances.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5047848224639893, 'label': 'Home&Garden>InteriorDecorating'}, {'relevance': 0.20000697672367096, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.10654819756746292, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.03153011202812195, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.025035366415977478, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.018540004268288612, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.018288733437657356, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.017766404896974564, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts'}, {'relevance': 0.014961646869778633, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.011533617973327637, 'label': 'FineArt>FineArtPhotography'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1891450, 'end': 1922290}, 'sentences_idx_start': 284, 'sentences_idx_end': 284}, {'text': 'And I think the reason this is really important to get on the table is because this distinction is kind of directly targeting the dynamic, shifting, very affective nature of affordances. So on the one hand, you have this landscape of affordances that is relatively static. So right now my landscape of affordances is Brighton. And the landscape of affordances in that sense is not really going to change very rapidly unless I kind of jump on a plane and go somewhere else.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.11624813824892044, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GovernmentBusiness'}, {'relevance': 0.10823478549718857, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.04784247651696205, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.04101058840751648, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.03958137333393097, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.036237213760614395, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.023601625114679337, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.01774374395608902, 'label': 'RealEstate>RealEstateBuyingAndSelling'}, {'relevance': 0.014148031361401081, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.011073868721723557, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Startups'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1922710, 'end': 1953018}, 'sentences_idx_start': 285, 'sentences_idx_end': 288}, {'text': "But the field of affordances has this thoroughly kind of normative, affective character to it. So depending on my internal state at any given time, depending on my expectations or my desires, say, my field of affordances is going to shift very rapidly. So not just predicated on my internal state, but also kind of contextual cues as well. So if something were to happen in the environment that was afforded very high precision weight in, then that's likely to shift my field of affordances significantly.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.13263164460659027, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}, {'relevance': 0.12125950306653976, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.04554533585906029, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.03701374679803848, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.03546757623553276, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.021173063665628433, 'label': 'RealEstate>RealEstateBuyingAndSelling'}, {'relevance': 0.010435686446726322, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.01002332754433155, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0060346489772200584, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.005817465949803591, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1953184, 'end': 1984710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 289, 'sentences_idx_end': 292}, {'text': "I think that the reason that I'm kind of emphasizing this to Darius's point is and kind of building on what Mark said, it doesn't seem like this distinction at least would apply from the perspective of the wall, say, because this kind of affectivity and normativity just isn't a feature of the wall's experience of the world. And also to kind of run with affordances. Perhaps you could say a bit more about how you would kind of think about this.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.4335038363933563, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.20463036000728607, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.01897430792450905, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.010643735527992249, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.009046252816915512, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>Painting'}, {'relevance': 0.006226932164281607, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005438054911792278, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.004549591336399317, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.004510832950472832, 'label': 'Home&Garden>InteriorDecorating'}, {'relevance': 0.0037212877068668604, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1986570, 'end': 2014926}, 'sentences_idx_start': 293, 'sentences_idx_end': 295}, {'text': "Darius because affordances are kind of opportunities for to. There's some debate about this, but I like to think of them as like a relational property between you have the skilled capabilities of an embodied agent and then you have some feature of the environment. So I think when you're thinking from the perspective of the wall, you have the features of the environment because you. Have the embodied characteristics of the agent are kind of playing that role.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.333809494972229, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.2100561559200287, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RealEstateIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.1277831643819809, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.033277787268161774, 'label': 'RealEstate>DevelopmentalSites'}, {'relevance': 0.031447380781173706, 'label': 'Home&Garden>IndoorEnvironmentalQuality'}, {'relevance': 0.03138560429215431, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>HousingMarket'}, {'relevance': 0.0252209585160017, 'label': 'RealEstate'}, {'relevance': 0.021578939631581306, 'label': 'RealEstate>OfficeProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.011035374365746975, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FrugalLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.008971961215138435, 'label': 'Home&Garden>InteriorDecorating'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2014948, 'end': 2043522}, 'sentences_idx_start': 296, 'sentences_idx_end': 299}, {'text': "But it's not clear to me what the kind of skilled capabilities of the wall is. So yeah, if you could just say a bit more about that. Yeah, I mean, it may be the case, as you pointed out, that actually the technical term affordance as being opportunities for action is misplaced.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01208655908703804, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.008854269050061703, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.005551632959395647, 'label': 'Home&Garden>InteriorDecorating'}, {'relevance': 0.0036813742481172085, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.0032158405520021915, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002965242601931095, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0023465256672352552, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.001934559317305684, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.0014928102027624846, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.0012200773926451802, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2043666, 'end': 2059450}, 'sentences_idx_start': 300, 'sentences_idx_end': 302}, {'text': "This is a lot of this I've been formulating, having read this very new paper by Ramsey and colleagues on Bayesian mechanics of physics of and by beliefs, where he really rams home this point, that the system, the generative model is the system of the kind of stochastic differential equations across the state space. So across the Marko blanca, across the particle with its Marko blanket and the external states. And that is the system which is in that system itself is in the business of reducing free energy.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.983683168888092, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.002564273774623871, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.001057592686265707, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00047028748667798936, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0004539312794804573, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00028802506858482957, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00026463394169695675, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00021984163322485983, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoBodyStyles>Microcar'}, {'relevance': 0.00019108920241706073, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ReproductiveHealth>Pregnancy'}, {'relevance': 0.00017682890756987035, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>Commodities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2061390, 'end': 2091638}, 'sentences_idx_start': 303, 'sentences_idx_end': 305}, {'text': "So it's not just the active inference agent, it's the whole system which is embedded in a whole system of other things. And so that was my general thinking, is that just on the prerequisite that these systems exist just on that a prior axiom, ther