ences_idx_end': 327}, {'text': 'So if you buy the frenzy principle and you also buy that it entails that agent have affordances or any approximal notion, then you also buy that walls have affordances. So there are basically three position you can have on that. One is that active inference is correct. Wall are fucking affordances and they do self evidencing, which I would not go with. Another option is that you have basically devolved in the detail. So, for example, maybe the adjunct environment is not the wall.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.016683422029018402, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Remodeling&Construction'}, {'relevance': 0.012432183139026165, 'label': 'Home&Garden>IndoorEnvironmentalQuality'}, {'relevance': 0.008830707520246506, 'label': 'RealEstate>RetailProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.008517839945852757, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>RealEstateIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0026056612841784954, 'label': 'RealEstate'}, {'relevance': 0.00207357294857502, 'label': 'RealEstate>Apartments'}, {'relevance': 0.001747304922901094, 'label': 'RealEstate>RealEstateBuyingAndSelling'}, {'relevance': 0.001429281197488308, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeImprovement'}, {'relevance': 0.0012505798367783427, 'label': 'RealEstate>Houses'}, {'relevance': 0.0011479618260636926, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2179214, 'end': 2217358}, 'sentences_idx_start': 328, 'sentences_idx_end': 333}, {'text': "It's something that is broader, like Gaia system, whatever, and it just happens. It includes the wall, but it is not the wall. And it does do self balancing. And the third is that active inference is wrong. We don't have affordances based on whatever is the formal presentation of active inference. And I would go in that direction of this phenomenology stuff. So we have, I would say, philosophical evidence in the sense that denying this would lead to nonsense.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.30532312393188477, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {