81, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0007259269477799535, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0006481001619249582, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0006117704906500876, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2542890, 'end': 2578246}, 'sentences_idx_start': 371, 'sentences_idx_end': 375}, {'text': "I know because you sent me the paper to review. Oh, yeah. Thank you. Early stages of a paper on the role of generative AI in classrooms. So, from the perspective of thinking about what kinds of affordance does generative AI represent in a learning environment, particularly, we're kind of applying active inference to classroom design and looking at it from the angles of different educational and pedagogical theories. But it's very early days. It probably depends on your view of generative II in general.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9933755993843079, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.21283553540706635, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.05843624472618103, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.04570954293012619, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.04189047962427139, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.017803329974412918, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01595529541373253, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.014270184561610222, 'label': 'Education>EarlyChildhoodEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.010985839180648327, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.007390225306153297, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2578268, 'end': 2623122}, 'sentences_idx_start': 376, 'sentences_idx_end': 382}, {'text': "I mean, it depends whether you would consider it a real cognitive agent or not. I think some people are more inclined to think of it as this is a thing that has agency, it has real understanding, and other people are maybe less inclined to think of it in those terms. And I think that might bear significantly on how you think of it. Yeah, that's super cool. That basically the last project you mentioned is very in line with my PhD project right now because my main PhD.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8241890668869019, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.026817724108695984, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.010262216441333294, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.004640707280486822, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003405414056032896, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0013797756982967257, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0013614181661978364, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.001187231857329607, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0006311673787422478, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006249823491089046, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2623176, 'end': 2655514}, 'sentences_idx_start': 383, 'sentences_idx_end': 387}, {'text': "Project is our European foundings, and it's about the AI for personalized education, and I'm trying to follow it through the active inference framework from a multi level perspective. Very cool. Yeah, we should we should probably talk more about that. Okay. Darius. Yeah? I wanted to ask I mean, this may be directed more mark so I know this is kind of his work in terms of slopes of uncertainty and about doing better than expected at reducing prediction error over time.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9626810550689697, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.751547634601593, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.07255018502473831, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.0674421563744545, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.01708301156759262, 'label': 'Education'}, {'relevance': 0.01625436544418335, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.01462372113019228, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.012904359959065914, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.008036105893552303, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EducationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.007138029206544161, 'label': 'Education>Homeschooling'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2655562, 'end': 2691820}, 'sentences_idx_start': 388, 'sentences_idx_end': 394}, {'text': "I was wondering kind of how the architecture of that is built into the particle, into the generative model because we have the kind of for me, I don't know if it's an hour and out sort of conflict, but we have these kind of implicit priors that we're going to fulfill certain expectations or minimize prediction error regarding certain things. Right. So homeostatic priors or happiness, well being, whatever it is.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.48526954650878906, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0115590151399374, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0018732411554083228, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.0011053687194362283, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0007499486673623323, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0004918008344247937, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.00043300940888002515, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.000386743777198717, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0003774667566176504, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0002875794598367065, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2692350, 'end': 2718850}, 'sentences_idx_start': 395, 'sentences_idx_end': 397}, {'text': "But then your claim is that we have the higher order beliefs, the higher order predictions that over and above, that I also need to do well, better than expected at reducing prediction error over time. So it's still quite fuzzy in my mind. But is there a kind of potential conflict there between the general priors that the system has and then actually, in a sense, violating those expectations by going over and above them, which itself constitutes an expectation? How do you kind of resolve that tension?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04338379576802254, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005437706597149372, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.004465457983314991, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.003627332393079996, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0024041917640715837, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.002209625905379653, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.001323249307461083, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.001136653358116746, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>MutualFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0008737393072806299, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0008706576772965491, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2719000, 'end': 2754110}, 'sentences_idx_start': 398, 'sentences_idx_end': 401}, {'text': "Yeah, that's interesting, but this is very much in Ben's wheelhouse too. Ben and I have been working on sloppy stuff for almost as long as I've been doing on his original paper called We'll Get It Up. They do a really good job of showing technically where this sits within a deep parametric model. Lara Senved Smith's paper on metacognition also does this by showing you have these depths of modeling where models above are modeling models below, and optimizing over those models below.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8376448750495911, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.001972674624994397, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0013468913966789842, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0011858083307743073, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0010874553117901087, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0008209984516724944, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006036270642653108, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.00044605418224819005, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002750451094470918, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.00020817785116378218, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2755810, 'end': 2806278}, 'sentences_idx_start': 402, 'sentences_idx_end': 405}, {'text': "So we have some good computational backbone for thinking, for not only thinking that this is the case, but beginning to express how it does the work it does. So let's leave that for digging into it, though, technically, sort of on our own, let me say sort of at a higher, more abstract level still, hopefully it's useful.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9807900190353394, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.6559346318244934, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.08827068656682968, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.028690090402960777, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.009650038555264473, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0031100797932595015, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002733912318944931, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002012354088947177, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.001733138575218618, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0014565892051905394, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2806364, 'end': 2826830}, 'sentences_idx_start': 406, 'sentences_idx_end': 407}, {'text': "It's not weird to think that this kind of anticipatory system is not only making predictions about the world, but it's also part of what it's predicting is how fast or slow, how efficient it is in particular contexts at resolving certain kinds of errors. That's a perfectly fine thing to think that we're also predicting slopes of engagement.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9868863224983215, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.024352464824914932, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.02234964445233345, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.007447340525686741, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.006913148798048496, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.005289463791996241, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.004957790020853281, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.004261938389390707, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.003407962154597044, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0032771991100162268, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2827490, 'end': 2849990}, 'sentences_idx_start': 408, 'sentences_idx_end': 409}, {'text': "And then all we're saying then is system also pays attention to when those expectations are breached and it's learning from those breaches that should just be the bread and butter for what the system does anyway. So precision is a second order process in much the same way precision is about how reliable are lower level predictions and then using that amount to toggle how impactful either errors or predictions are.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.715055525302887, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.004383972380310297, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.0022901631891727448, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>AntivirusSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0013991418527439237, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0006502764881588519, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0004065422690473497, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Disasters'}, {'relevance': 0.00037532910937443376, 'label': 'Home&Garden>HomeSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.000355164404027164, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.00021110936359036714, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.00019347938359715044, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2851050, 'end': 2882318}, 'sentences_idx_start': 410, 'sentences_idx_end': 411}, {'text': "So we've already got baked into the system, right from early days, this idea that the system is not only making predictions, but monitoring its own predictive processing regimes and then toggling based on how reliable those substreams are.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.28546592593193054, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0438091866672039, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.04138287529349327, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.007760837208479643, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.005106141325086355, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0038907506968826056, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0026699656154960394, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0024555844720453024, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.002045172266662121, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0017985155573114753, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2882404, 'end': 2897860}, 'sentences_idx_start': 412, 'sentences_idx_end': 412}, {'text': "All we're adding here is when we first thought about those mechanisms, one thing that can happen, this is just good for everybody who's interested in active inference, because I bump into this with my students all the time when we say something like precision weighting, a tendency to think of thing. So we go to find this precision like where's the biological or precision weighting?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05872108042240143, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.004046620335429907, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.0015036443946883082, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0011032725451514125, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.000585838919505477, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.000568280927836895, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.0005572676309384406, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.00047533796168863773, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0003576577000785619, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.0003504489432089031, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2898310, 'end': 2924566}, 'sentences_idx_start': 413, 'sentences_idx_end': 414}, {'text': "But when we actually get into a biosystem and we look for these things, the truth is precision is going to be weighted in lots of different ways. I mean, that's the real frontier of this research is to actually find how these things are instantiated and the answer is going to be multifarious. I mean, you're going to have precision adjustments happening throughout the system in lots of ways. It could be synchrony and asynchronous and desynchronies between systems.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9476858377456665, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.3963666558265686, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>BiotechAndBiomedicalIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.024631725624203682, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.021856648847460747, 'label': 'Science>Genetics'}, {'relevance': 0.010478969663381577, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}, {'relevance': 0.0028520298656076193, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EnvironmentalServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001277793780900538, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0005598146817646921, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>InfectiousDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.0004932583542540669, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MechanicalAndIndustrialEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0004351286042947322, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HerbsAndSupplements'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2924598, 'end': 2947042}, 'sentences_idx_start': 415, 'sentences_idx_end': 418}, {'text': "It can be neuromodulatory chemicals, it can be structural shapes within the brain. I mean, precision is going to be set in lots of different ways. So all that we're pointing out here is that one of the ways that precision is being set, one of the ways that the system is tracking how efficient it is and then upping or lowering the amount of impact error signals or predictions have, is that it's happening in an embodied way.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3332849144935608, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.13388657569885254, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.029481982812285423, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.008061971515417099, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0075176008976995945, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0024332415778189898, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0021836471278220415, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.002141157630831003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0014076440129429102, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0012255148030817509, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2947106, 'end': 2983486}, 'sentences_idx_start': 419, 'sentences_idx_end': 421}, {'text': "So we've looked over to the effective search and lo and behold, there are all these signatures that we were looking for for this part of the machinery. So not weird that the system is tracking its own regularities and adjusting. That was baked in right from the beginning. How it does that, that's one of the frontiers. It's going to happen in lots of different ways. Lo and behold.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0429748073220253, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.030827326700091362, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.008523455820977688, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.006907857023179531, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.005211082752794027, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.004748880863189697, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Search'}, {'relevance': 0.0012470107758417726, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.00106948078610003, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>AntivirusSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.000997075461782515, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007399003370665014, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 2983588, 'end': 3008594}, 'sentences_idx_start': 422, 'sentences_idx_end': 427}, {'text': "Affect the dynamics, the shoe fits, they look like they do that stuff and then you bring it to the lab and you go back to like reward prediction error research and sure enough, neuromodulatory chemicals, reward systems are tuning affective dynamics relative to better than and worse than slopes of uncertainty management. It's exactly what we would expect given the computational model.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1944100558757782, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.07573577016592026, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.05098668113350868, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.01905246265232563, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.004396532196551561, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004234137944877148, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases'}, {'relevance': 0.002615633886307478, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>Menopause'}, {'relevance': 0.0016102154040709138, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.001257089083082974, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0010246016317978501, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>MMOs'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3008642, 'end': 3031760}, 'sentences_idx_start': 428, 'sentences_idx_end': 429}, {'text': "So then it was an easy next step to start saying, well look, there's one of the ways that precision, there's one of the ways that affect system. Now just notice there it's the only precision, it's not the only thing the affected system is doing. We never want to say we're careful not to be reductionist to say, oh, affect is always aerodynamics. I don't think that's right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004711593501269817, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoParts'}, {'relevance': 0.0038548398297280073, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>ConceptCars'}, {'relevance': 0.00291207293048501, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.002050601877272129, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017256350256502628, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AviationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001355168642476201, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0013010009424760938, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>RadioControl'}, {'relevance': 0.0010613802587613463, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00099774484988302, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MechanicalAndIndustrialEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0008161549922078848, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3032290, 'end': 3058678}, 'sentences_idx_start': 430, 'sentences_idx_end': 433}, {'text': "I think it's that aerodynamics are expressed in part effectively and they have this impact on the system that we've known about for a long time, even from just the reward prediction error literature. Does that help or was that a bit is that okay? Yeah, just to add two things really quickly there because I know time is kind of catching up with us.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09100133180618286, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.004789377097040415, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AviationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004246431868523359, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0037613268941640854, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AirTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0020392148289829493, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0018434567609801888, 'label': 'Sports>FantasySports'}, {'relevance': 0.001829541171900928, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoSafety'}, {'relevance': 0.0014667531941086054, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.0013088269624859095, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0011386533733457327, 'label': 'Sports>AutoRacing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3058764, 'end': 3083950}, 'sentences_idx_start': 434, 'sentences_idx_end': 436}, {'text': "I would emphasize as well, just as a kind of general .1 of the things I really like about the work on aerodynamics and affect is it has this nice kind of broad capture of the kinds of affectivity that agents can experience. So when we talk about affectivity, we're not just talking about full blooded emotions or even just moods, but we're talking about what?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.009657871909439564, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.006724804639816284, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>AviationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.006148211658000946, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0060339998453855515, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AirTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.005137749016284943, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>RadioControl'}, {'relevance': 0.004418875556439161, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0029743651393800974, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0022703357972204685, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoSafety'}, {'relevance': 0.0022086810786277056, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0017812686273828149, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoSafetyTechnologies'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3084020, 'end': 3106934}, 'sentences_idx_start': 437, 'sentences_idx_end': 438}, {'text': "One of the things I kind of drew attention to in the lecture was Matthew Ratcliffe's work on existential feelings, which I think is just such the connection between active inference and phenomenology that you find in some of this work is just insanely powerful. And it's one of the things that really drew me into the framework the second thing, just building one thing that I don't think I mentioned in the lecture is active inference. It has been described as a quintessentially metacognitive framework.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3671764135360718, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.12187554687261581, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.09966301172971725, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.07458280771970749, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.017215358093380928, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.008962888270616531, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0046324413269758224, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.003791697323322296, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0018559102900326252, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.001585370278917253, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3107052, 'end': 3138190}, 'sentences_idx_start': 439, 'sentences_idx_end': 441}, {'text': "So you have kind of built into the architecture, you have expectations over expect, so you have kind of predictions about predictions and this has proved to be just, again, just phenomenally useful for thinking about certain aspects of phenomenology as well. So yeah, I think that these are like real strengths of the framework. Okay, I don't know how we're doing for time. Are we strictly limited on or can we we are not as far as I know.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.432257741689682, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.00598517619073391, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.004278283566236496, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.003868578467518091, 'label': 'Science>SpaceAndAstronomy'}, {'relevance': 0.003391064004972577, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002319247927516699, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0011420241789892316, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007161098183132708, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007097113411873579, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0007036646129563451, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3138350, 'end': 3177190}, 'sentences_idx_start': 442, 'sentences_idx_end': 445}, {'text': "Daniel well, I can probably do I definitely do another 15 if anybody has any more questions. And people, I should say as well, that doesn't mean that we're all held captive to my time frame. So if people do need to leave within the next five or ten minutes, that's absolutely fine, but I'm certainly happy to carry on if anybody has any more questions or comments.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0030069679487496614, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}, {'relevance': 0.002270684577524662, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Camping'}, {'relevance': 0.002216944471001625, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0014894045889377594, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0014499243116006255, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.0012449127389118075, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>FanConventions'}, {'relevance': 0.0010913542937487364, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0009125020587816834, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0008872092003002763, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>TalkRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.0007337064016610384, 'label': 'Television>SpecialInterestTV'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3177800, 'end': 3202620}, 'sentences_idx_start': 446, 'sentences_idx_end': 448}, {'text': "If no one else has got any, I would quite like to go back to earlier in the discussion you were talking about the value of uncertainty because in organizations in which I'm working with, we often have conversations about uncertainty and what we find is over time there tends to be a drift towards risk aversion. So we're working with a large international construction company at the Minute, and they used to have a culture in which innovation was quite well embedded.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3331618309020996, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Startups'}, {'relevance': 0.21195246279239655, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.18273843824863434, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ConstructionIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.16216926276683807, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.1295258104801178, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.02400495670735836, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>VentureCapital'}, {'relevance': 0.010749908164143562, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ManagementConsultingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.009496866725385189, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.007656956557184458, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>AngelInvestment'}, {'relevance': 0.007603781763464212, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3207060, 'end': 3242312}, 'sentences_idx_start': 449, 'sentences_idx_end': 450}, {'text': "And over time, it's kind of drifted towards very, very risk averse culture where actually, rather than learning through the process and being able to tolerate uncertainty around opportunities and what can be accomplished and that kind of surveillance that comes with the intrinsic reward, I suppose, of being able to reduce uncertainty about capabilities to a situation where they're trying to anticipate all of the risks upfront before they even get involved in the project. So there's some kind of valence switch.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3471051752567291, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.29629144072532654, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.03523195907473564, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ConstructionIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.015108347870409489, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ManagementConsultingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.013008900918066502, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Startups'}, {'relevance': 0.008388417772948742, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.006424705032259226, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.006185118108987808, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>GovernmentBusiness'}, {'relevance': 0.003911699168384075, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0038301667664200068, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3242376, 'end': 3273616}, 'sentences_idx_start': 451, 'sentences_idx_end': 452}, {'text': "Mark and you mentioned David Blaine earlier and something about the context there was a switch in valence from yeah, this is a kind of a play, this is a safe thing to do, to actually know this has real consequences. So I'd like to explore that a little bit more actually, if anyone's got kind of any insights or papers or comments. Yeah, I think that's a really interesting question, actually.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.25633078813552856, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityScandal'}, {'relevance': 0.1307300329208374, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Fiction'}, {'relevance': 0.12761190533638, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.07299890369176865, 'label': 'Movies>DocumentaryMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.06935147196054459, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.060303330421447754, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.05763190612196922, 'label': 'Television>DramaTV'}, {'relevance': 0.04393662512302399, 'label': 'Movies>DramaMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.04101313650608063, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0320776104927063, 'label': 'PopCulture>HumorAndSatire'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3273728, 'end': 3303090}, 'sentences_idx_start': 453, 'sentences_idx_end': 455}, {'text': "It seems like one of the things we've been talking about is this connection between uncertainty, prediction, error, minimization and affectivity in individual agents. And it sounds like what you're asking is how does that translate to collectives? So one of the things about active inference that we're going to see in subsequent weeks is how it scales up to kind of larger systems like companies or groups that are trying to achieve some kind of shared goal.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9057298302650452, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.007798830512911081, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.006606943905353546, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0053338040597736835, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.003705226117745042, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0028057151939719915, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.002655284944921732, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0025674698408693075, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0017535798251628876, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0017339783953502774, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3304900, 'end': 3338360}, 'sentences_idx_start': 456, 'sentences_idx_end': 458}, {'text': "How does the value of uncertainty translate onto how is it scalable in that sense? Right? Would that be a fair kind of yeah, I guess so. Uncertainty often when it's talked about uncertainty is talked about as risk, which is, I suppose, is predictions or anticipation of outcomes that we don't want. Right. Whereas there's also positive uncertainty, which is, I suppose, simply stated opportunities through curiosity.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01774665340781212, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.010742300190031528, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Startups'}, {'relevance': 0.009855881333351135, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.004728667438030243, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>AngelInvestment'}, {'relevance': 0.0037342561408877373, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>VentureCapital'}, {'relevance': 0.003552190260961652, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0029672677628695965, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0025182419922202826, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0013444933574646711, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0009719650261104107, 'label': 'Science'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3339820, 'end': 3375824}, 'sentences_idx_start': 459, 'sentences_idx_end': 464}, {'text': "What might we be able to achieve this kind of novelty seeking, I guess that new opportunities that we haven't exploited, and they're just in the kind of organizational systems. I think there are various pressures that cause it, but over time, you see these cultural shifts towards a very kind of risk averse where the valence is obviously quite negative, quite an unpleasant feeling for people. Yeah, this is good. This is right at the heart of my current work. I'm really interested.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6900730729103088, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.17346125841140747, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.10053901374340057, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.09343402087688446, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.08133284747600555, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.07302451133728027, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Startups'}, {'relevance': 0.04699328914284706, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.03174741566181183, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>ManagementConsultingIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.02318735420703888, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.022107833996415138, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3375952, 'end': 3412608}, 'sentences_idx_start': 465, 'sentences_idx_end': 469}, {'text': "So we just had a big stint where active inference models were starting to be used in computational psychiatry, especially for pathological disorders. So addiction, depression, disassociative disorders, OCD PTSD. It's quite a sexy framework for thinking about some of the ways that the cognitive system breaks down and the sort of new move right now. I mean, we have a collection coming out right now in Neuroscience of Consciousness.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7216885089874268, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.40662315487861633, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.36469221115112305, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.11566253006458282, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.04958900064229965, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.011604337953031063, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.009209774434566498, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.005368291400372982, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004078622441738844, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0029999883845448494, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3412694, 'end': 3437860}, 'sentences_idx_start': 470, 'sentences_idx_end': 473}, {'text': "Is to think about these things in terms of, okay, if we are predictive systems and we have a sufficiently rich model of how that system works in a particular niche, what sorts of ways can we intervene on that system in order to have positive outcomes, rather than just modeling what the negative outcomes are? And I hear that a lot in what you're saying now. So I'm just going to drop one link for you there.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.4728843569755554, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.016581688076257706, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>MarketingAndAdvertising'}, {'relevance': 0.007824006490409374, 'label': 'Careers>JobSearch'}, {'relevance': 0.007168970070779324, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.005352349020540714, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>JobMarket'}, {'relevance': 0.005173227284103632, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.005029702093452215, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.004692956805229187, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.003776582656428218, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>HealthcareIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.003316954942420125, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3437940, 'end': 3460976}, 'sentences_idx_start': 474, 'sentences_idx_end': 476}, {'text': "This is Casper Hess again wrote a very small paper with a nice little model called Sophisticated Affective Inference. Here's a little bot that tends towards catastrophe catastrophizing the future. If it's given like, fun medium fun medium fun dangerous. Over time, it tends to expect the dangerous one. Like after 10,000 iterations, it basically lives in the worst possible scenario, which is a nice little this is my wife, this is most people today.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5810950994491577, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Disasters'}, {'relevance': 0.11058541387319565, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.011553279124200344, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0072066690772771835, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.006342493928968906, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.0046665421687066555, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0035934080369770527, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0028857188299298286, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries>FirstAid'}, {'relevance': 0.0018018699483945966, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoSafety'}, {'relevance': 0.0017931159818544984, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>WarAndConflicts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3461078, 'end': 3497260}, 'sentences_idx_start': 477, 'sentences_idx_end': 481}, {'text': "So the question is, I want to know, given the model, why does that happen and what can we be doing to intervene? And part of the answer is going to be we need to become more tolerant of uncertainty. That's one of the things that the system can be better or worse at. So this just takes the computational modeling and then looks to things that we already know about emotional regulation. That's part of the story.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8961071968078613, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.04646158963441849, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.022556928917765617, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting'}, {'relevance': 0.013523654080927372, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.013301364146173, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0065750544890761375, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005414939485490322, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0025172673631459475, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.002402797108516097, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.0022580609656870365, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>Menopause'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3497410, 'end': 3522310}, 'sentences_idx_start': 482, 'sentences_idx_end': 486}, {'text': "So we've done a little bit of work on this with our predictive dynamics of happiness and wellbeing, and Ryan Smith is definitely doing work on this with active inference and well being. So definitely check that out if you're interested here. I'll just flag one interesting thing here that relates just to what we were just talking about, about layers of modeling. One way that let's say two ways. There's two ways that a system, and it's probably going to be lots.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.851499080657959, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness'}, {'relevance': 0.5196377635002136, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.07403522729873657, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.013405682519078255, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00850500725209713, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.008361983112990856, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.007883219048380852, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.007497643120586872, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.006525527685880661, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00520293228328228, 'label': 'MedicalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3523480, 'end': 3550776}, 'sentences_idx_start': 487, 'sentences_idx_end': 491}, {'text': 'But the two that come to mind that a system can become more tolerant to uncertainty is one exposure. So this is why exposure therapy might be useful for our kind of a system. You want to expose the system to volatility at the lower and middle levels of the hierarchy and have it turn out okay. So that one of the things that the system can come to predict is not only particular outcomes, but it can also predict how much error is involved in particular outcomes.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02745784819126129, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.008254142478108406, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0075915297493338585, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.004322961438447237, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.004277595318853855, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialCrisis'}, {'relevance': 0.0035170288756489754, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.003466462716460228, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0032286043278872967, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0026570241898298264, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.002332270611077547, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3550808, 'end': 3579588}, 'sentences_idx_start': 492, 'sentences_idx_end': 495}, {'text': "So, for instance, when I used to give a pro talk, I was always really nervous, and I don't know if that ever really went away, but I've had so much exposure to the anxiety of giving a professional talk that basically I don't notice it anymore. But if you were to ask me at the beginning of my talk, mark right now, what's your phenomenology? And I sort of meditatively looked, I'd probably say, yeah, I'm nervous.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.005784695502370596, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.005639477167278528, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0014933597994968295, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0012752217007800937, 'label': 'Education>CollegeEducation>PostgraduateEducation>ProfessionalSchool'}, {'relevance': 0.0012651990400627255, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.0010168503504246473, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0009484157781116664, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>ComedyEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.0008948940085247159, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0008211491513065994, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0007790842792019248, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3579684, 'end': 3604536}, 'sentences_idx_start': 496, 'sentences_idx_end': 498}, {'text': "But if you hadn't have said that and you were just like, hey, what's up? I've been like, oh yeah, I'm great. It's all good. I don't even notice it anymore. That's because the system knows that I have errors go up, but as soon as I start talking, they drop away. And because I know the arc that even error in the system, it becomes non newsworthy.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.004209762904793024, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ConsumerIssues>Recalls'}, {'relevance': 0.0030058601405471563, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoRecalls'}, {'relevance': 0.0026859166100621223, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0022944314405322075, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>Email'}, {'relevance': 0.0015389096224680543, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.0012548879021778703, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment>StandardizedTesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0012517643626779318, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>NationalNews'}, {'relevance': 0.0009459348511882126, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoSafety'}, {'relevance': 0.0008826063713058829, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityScandal'}, {'relevance': 0.0007789494702592492, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>InternationalNews'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3604648, 'end': 3622256}, 'sentences_idx_start': 499, 'sentences_idx_end': 504}, {'text': "It's no longer interesting volatility to be tracking that's just from exposure. So what's happening is you're having errors at a lower or middle level that a higher level is now modeling, saying when we come here, we should expect this arc of error. Same thing when you work out like real gym rats, they can feel good.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5383877754211426, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.06050581857562065, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.006596239283680916, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.0037973823491483927, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.002379437442868948, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0006203827215358615, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.0005002105026505888, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialCrisis'}, {'relevance': 0.00032778954482637346, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SportsVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.00028434491832740605, 'label': 'Sports'}, {'relevance': 0.0002774925669655204, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3622288, 'end': 3639370}, 'sentences_idx_start': 505, 'sentences_idx_end': 507}, {'text': "You're having your system right, but at the higher level, it's now learned not only that that has a natural arc, but that that's a good sign at a higher level. So now you're getting positive prediction error slope high and negative prediction error slope low. Okay, so one exposure. Two, you can model your own responses. This is something Ben and I work on with horror movies. You can take an active role in mindfully observing your own reactions to volatility.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04668557271361351, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.03308524563908577, 'label': 'Movies>HorrorMovies'}, {'relevance': 0.009356645867228508, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.007996765896677971, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.0034199499059468508, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.0028130582068115473, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0014058896340429783, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0010550909209996462, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0009760982356965542, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.0008699147147126496, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3642400, 'end': 3682900}, 'sentences_idx_start': 508, 'sentences_idx_end': 513}, {'text': "And this comes up in our paper on horror. We've already dropped the link today if you want to check it out. Something really special happens when the system models its own reaction to volatility. It starts to learn that even reactions to volatility, they don't need to be compounded up into dangers, that it's okay to be uncertain at certain levels of the system. So how that translates into business, I'm not sure, other than I know tolerance to uncertainty is a marker of business success.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7064382433891296, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.19517366588115692, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.13042698800563812, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialCrisis'}, {'relevance': 0.06555149704217911, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>InterestRates'}, {'relevance': 0.06487398594617844, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.05356229469180107, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>HedgeFunds'}, {'relevance': 0.012552264146506786, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>FinancialIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.007014585193246603, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialReform'}, {'relevance': 0.002803297247737646, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0021034658420830965, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>FinancialRegulation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3683060, 'end': 3711650}, 'sentences_idx_start': 514, 'sentences_idx_end': 518}, {'text': "And I suspect the framework in a fit with lots of mindfulness work about learning to tolerate uncertainty. Is there anything about the role of language in kind of modulating those metacognitive? Oh, it's good. If I may, I was preparing an answer on that specifically, and I was nervously waiting for opportunity. Sorry, Mark. Meta in terms of evolutionary cognitive archaeology, we don't know when language emerge, but we do know that, let's say an encouraging semantic system.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9749348163604736, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.5589285492897034, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.03295323997735977, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.008563308045268059, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0043077836744487286, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.003114599734544754, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.002853327663615346, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002004030393436551, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.001823858474381268, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0018232326256111264, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3712180, 'end': 3753708}, 'sentences_idx_start': 519, 'sentences_idx_end': 524}, {'text': "So you can build things in language, and you can expect things in the world to correspond to things in language. So, for example, if you that's abstract, as I say, it's abstract, but you can, for example, have a self identity, and I'm a French, and I communicate with the expectation that are embedded in that identity with other people. And that means we communicate over norms. So we have specific expectation of what we will do.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9198394417762756, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.0776435136795044, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.02469443343579769, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.006372178439050913, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0025025629438459873, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0019222779665142298, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0015787661541253328, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0010106338886544108, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0009134297724813223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007218560785986483, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Poetry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3753794, 'end': 3781656}, 'sentences_idx_start': 525, 'sentences_idx_end': 528}, {'text': 'And those expectations, they become embedded in specific symbolic markers that are embedded in language. And something that the thing that it was strongly evoked in my mind when you talked of tolerance to insecurity is that as far as documented history goes, Europeans well, Indo Europeans, they are pretty strong on the idea that things have a nature and they act lawfully. And their nature and their laws, they somehow correspond to linguistic categories.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8185833692550659, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.7730743885040283, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.4054180085659027, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.3100391924381256, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>WarAndConflicts'}, {'relevance': 0.17676906287670135, 'label': 'Travel>TravelLocations>EuropeTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.04421328753232956, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Crime'}, {'relevance': 0.023293687030673027, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Law'}, {'relevance': 0.004338054917752743, 'label': 'Science>Geography'}, {'relevance': 0.0031041100155562162, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy'}, {'relevance': 0.002695166040211916, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3781838, 'end': 3819760}, 'sentences_idx_start': 529, 'sentences_idx_end': 531}, {'text': "So I can say stuff like chickens quack, and that's a proper explanation of what are chicken and why they quack. And if you look in Chinese philosophy, as far as written history goes, you have a much accent on Wei Wu Wei. So a poor translation would be effortless action. Closer translation would be action without action.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.15049801766872406, 'label': 'Pets>Birds'}, {'relevance': 0.017117634415626526, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Beekeeping'}, {'relevance': 0.012612040154635906, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Birdwatching'}, {'relevance': 0.001077650929801166, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ColdAndFlu'}, {'relevance': 0.0006350516923703253, 'label': 'Pets>Cats'}, {'relevance': 0.0004912217846140265, 'label': 'Sports>HuntingAndShooting'}, {'relevance': 0.00029910061857663095, 'label': 'Pets>LargeAnimals'}, {'relevance': 0.0002797971828840673, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0002601529413368553, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0002320511848665774, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3819920, 'end': 3850296}, 'sentences_idx_start': 532, 'sentences_idx_end': 535}, {'text': "So it's something that is quite close to the phenomenology of flow in that you observe yourself doing things and you do not apply a conscious effort to the flow of what you're doing. And that looks like something that is closer to the phenomenology you'd expect.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07647575438022614, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.07381981611251831, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0032486801501363516, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.002656509866937995, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0015957951545715332, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015276530757546425, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.000991352368146181, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006970459362491965, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0006722900434397161, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0005073501961305737, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3850488, 'end': 3871332}, 'sentences_idx_start': 536, 'sentences_idx_end': 537}, {'text': "If you apply recursive preactive cognition with less or less heavy or more effectively integrated symbolic concurring like use of language as something that you actually expect to be meaningful and to constrain strongly your actions and marginally, I'd expect, very strongly expect that linguistic categories will map and what you build with it. So, I don't know, self identities, plans, whatever will map cleanly onto what you observe. You will be very anxious about things, because that does not happen usually.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9531945586204529, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.24770602583885193, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.03151798993349075, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.010164192877709866, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.002127436688169837, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0016526159597560763, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.001307582831941545, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0012321473332121968, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0009443464805372059, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0009005632600747049, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3871386, 'end': 3907570}, 'sentences_idx_start': 538, 'sentences_idx_end': 540}, {'text': "And yeah, besides grand discourse on interpret traits, which are usually not that constructive sorry, I got lost because I did not let me just say one thing before we move off this point. A simple way that language might help is by invoking cognitive flexibility. So oftentimes we think about the management of error being either updating predictions or acting on the world. That's the dyad. Usually what it overlooks is the third one, which is we can also manage volatility by redeploying precision in a better way.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0032107301522046328, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.002086268039420247, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>Options'}, {'relevance': 0.0018982369219884276, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.001801640959456563, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.00138897355645895, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0010011651320382953, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0009999593021348119, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0009161339257843792, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0008336066966876388, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.0007378770387731493, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3910020, 'end': 3951868}, 'sentences_idx_start': 541, 'sentences_idx_end': 545}, {'text': "So rather than just updating your model to fit the world or updating the world to fit your model, you can just change the set of what matters so that you're not really updating the model and you're not really changing the world. You're just changing the problem landscape. And that's something language allows us to do. It's maybe one of the really amazing things that language allows us to do is we can use language to bootstrap that kind of precision adjustment.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8632018566131592, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.013593212701380253, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.01265348307788372, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.008184630423784256, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDevelopment'}, {'relevance': 0.00474205706268549, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>Databases'}, {'relevance': 0.0043764738366007805, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0033230548724532127, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>WebDesignAndHTML'}, {'relevance': 0.001857325085438788, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0017873834585770965, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.000923153362236917, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3952034, 'end': 3976832}, 'sentences_idx_start': 546, 'sentences_idx_end': 549}, {'text': "So if the train doesn't come on time, we both notice it. Okay. And we feel bad that's perceptual updating. We might go and get a taxi that's active updating. But I might just say to you, wow, look, isn't it lovely that now we get a little bit more time to read our book or to continue our conversation or let's finish our coffee with a little bit of ease. I mean, we get an extra 20 minutes.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.19145168364048004, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>RailTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.01200264971703291, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.01091590616852045, 'label': 'Sports>Cycling'}, {'relevance': 0.004455160815268755, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AirTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0014041869435459375, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0013782974565401673, 'label': 'Automotive>Road-SideAssistance'}, {'relevance': 0.000575278652831912, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}, {'relevance': 0.0004544055846054107, 'label': 'RealEstate>OfficeProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.0003223132516723126, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.00031935152946971357, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3976896, 'end': 3998060}, 'sentences_idx_start': 550, 'sentences_idx_end': 555}, {'text': "Now even just saying that redeploys precision over the problem. Space now the train being late isn't volatility in the system. The train being late is signaling to the system that a better than expected slope has been achieved. Isn't that so interesting? The exact same occurrence is either undigestible volatility, right, like you're going to be late. Oh my goodness.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5032878518104553, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>RailTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0023646026384085417, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.000604102504439652, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AirTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0002634409174788743, 'label': 'Sports>EquineSports>HorseRacing'}, {'relevance': 0.0002604745968710631, 'label': 'Sports>Cycling'}, {'relevance': 0.00018515139527153224, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology>AutoNavigationSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.00015804391296114773, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>ReproductiveHealth>Pregnancy'}, {'relevance': 0.00015178807370830327, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>CollegeRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.0001499546051491052, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Economy>GasolinePrices'}, {'relevance': 0.0001477192563470453, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>GreenVehicles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3998130, 'end': 4019600}, 'sentences_idx_start': 556, 'sentences_idx_end': 561}, {'text': "Or it's an opportunity for an improvement in the system, which is now you get more time with the person that you're taking the train with. And that was just a matter of linguistic perturbance of the way that precision is being looking at. If you wanted to dig into the research here, I would look up cognitive flexibility and language or coaching cognitive flexibility is such a good point here. So you have a paper by Nick Clark on this specific encouraging role of language.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8815223574638367, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.03702258691191673, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.019188305363059044, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.009019405581057072, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.006105248350650072, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>LogisticsAndTransportationIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004513937048