entences_idx_end': 570}, {'text': "And so that is an extremely powerful encouraging system because I just have to tell a plan to myself and boom, that pushes me, nudges me nicely throughout the plan. But then you can have a different level of meta expectation over how language corresponds to reality. And I'd say a very strong factor of aversion to uncertainty is whether you expect your plans or your linguistic structure to nicely map onto reality because it will not happen.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.810236930847168, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.008282890543341637, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.00679326057434082, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.003364111064001918, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.003227740526199341, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.002594761550426483, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0020645807962864637, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0018200019840151072, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.001446387032046914, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0012441629078239202, 'label': 'Education>EarlyChildhoodEducation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4081198, 'end': 4109664}, 'sentences_idx_start': 571, 'sentences_idx_end': 573}, {'text': "But if you expect strongly that it will be the case, you will have to make it happen somehow. And here you will adapt rigid strategies and you will lose flexibility, but also language necessary for flexibility to be the case in the first place. So it's about coupling between dimension of cognition. Yeah. And I would just kind of risk and danger are two things that I've been really interested in across a kind of variety of different contexts. And I would say some of the.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.0736529678106308, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.01137495692819357, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.009430269710719585, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.005805844906717539, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.002253093523904681, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0021487439516931772, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>WarAndConflicts'}, {'relevance': 0.002124352613463998, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0020606538746505976, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0020452647004276514, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0018260534852743149, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4109782, 'end': 4145548}, 'sentences_idx_start': 574, 'sentences_idx_end': 579}, {'text': "Things that have been said like how you can influence the system by externalizing things through language and the different strategies that systems, whatever scale they're on, have minimizing prediction error, minimizing free energy. But also I would just emphasize the importance of external context here as well. So even in the case of a collective like a business, you still have to take into account the environment in which the business is operating. And I've been really interested in a particularly extreme example of context.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.23600651323795319, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.14006805419921875, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0343526154756546, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>InformationAndNetworkSecurity'}, {'relevance': 0.03207320347428322, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.030223878100514412, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.025522006675601006, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.013295314274728298, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.00938235130161047, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.007698421366512775, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00407834118232131, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4145554, 'end': 4177100}, 'sentences_idx_start': 580, 'sentences_idx_end': 583}, {'text': "I used to still do some work in philosophy of sport and I've been really interested in dangerous sports and why there seems to be this insane contextual effect where within a very kind of narrow contextual band of sporting practice, people seem willing to take on risks that outside of that context would just be completely insane.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9855942130088806, 'label': 'Sports'}, {'relevance': 0.7186800837516785, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.4899117052555084, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>SportingEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.3466411530971527, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise>ParticipantSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0605236291885376, 'label': 'Sports>SportsEquipment'}, {'relevance': 0.012834209017455578, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Injuries'}, {'relevance': 0.007950469851493835, 'label': "Style&Fashion>Women'sFashion>Women'sClothing>Women'sSportswear"}, {'relevance': 0.005861952900886536, 'label': 'Sports>DisabledSports'}, {'relevance': 0.004367318470031023, 'label': 'Sports>TrackAndField'}, {'relevance': 0.0036452647764235735, 'label': 'Sports>CollegeSports'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4177280, 'end': 4199020}, 'sentences_idx_start': 584, 'sentences_idx_end': 584}, {'text': "And I think this is something that's probably going to come up again in subsequent weeks as well here when we talk about the way that expectations on an individual or a collective basis can be set through other minds. So what somebody else expect myself to do? And so on and so on. Darius, you've had your hand up a while. Do you want to jump in? Yes, please.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3979564309120178, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.019120212644338608, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.008834167383611202, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.004292881116271019, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.003307105740532279, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.003236207878217101, 'label': 'Careers>CareerPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.002844810951501131, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>HumanResources'}, {'relevance': 0.002581092994660139, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting>StocksAndBonds'}, {'relevance': 0.002575875027105212, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0022026991937309504, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4199680, 'end': 4229960}, 'sentences_idx_start': 585, 'sentences_idx_end': 590}, {'text': "I'm not sure this is the sort of grand synthesis of any of this, but flow was mentioned. As I said, it's a kind of pet topic of mine and something that we know about flow. And this is why it's integrated into this idea of language and agency, is that at least in its original conception, success, mahali, and the sort of qualitative experience associated with flow, you would find stuff like not only the dilation of time, but also the reduction in self consciousness.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7788317203521729, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.07035122066736221, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.052949756383895874, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.008293150924146175, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.004720304161310196, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.004671689588576555, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0024114397820085287, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0023863203823566437, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Poetry'}, {'relevance': 0.0023826363030821085, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.0021996712312102318, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4230030, 'end': 4262268}, 'sentences_idx_start': 591, 'sentences_idx_end': 593}, {'text': "And now this is sort of picking up a lot of work that happens at UCL and people like Jeremy Skipper how integrated language is into the sense of self. And it seems to me, and this is kind of shooting from the hip, that all of these very deep rooted, I guess they're kind of psychotechnologies the self language seem to dissipate at this goldilocks zone, at this point of at this edge of criticality, at this flow state.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9191128611564636, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.13545392453670502, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.039935823529958725, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Poetry'}, {'relevance': 0.013819758780300617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.013016966171562672, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.009966311976313591, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.007652841974049807, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0074457405135035515, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.006621954496949911, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.005640718154609203, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4262444, 'end': 4290510}, 'sentences_idx_start': 594, 'sentences_idx_end': 595}, {'text': "Which makes me think if the flow state is a phenomenological offshoot of being optimally reducing prediction error, what is the kind of role of the concept of the self or linguistic functions? Because it seems to me that that becomes a regulatory function when that optimality is reduced, when stuff starts going wrong. So I think you can also think about this in the kind of Heideggerian or draythe's sense of just opening a door. You only start to represent the door in yourself.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.014918621629476547, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0023684650659561157, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.002324627246707678, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.0017468675505369902, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0010074303718283772, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.0010045282542705536, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Weather'}, {'relevance': 0.0008996413671411574, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>PersonalInvesting'}, {'relevance': 0.000792181643191725, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0007890519918873906, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0007095428882166743, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4291040, 'end': 4321988}, 'sentences_idx_start': 596, 'sentences_idx_end': 599}, {'text': "You only give it the linguistic object of a door when you can't open it. When you open a door standard, there is no representation going there. I mean, you could even argue there's no qualia there. So I'm wondering how deep that runs and what we can say about the role of agency, selfhood, maybe even consciousness because they don't seem to be that prevalent, at least from my understanding. When we are at the edge of criticality.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09141326695680618, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.04355601221323013, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.036638274788856506, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.034529589116573334, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.008110609836876392, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.006114322692155838, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Atheism'}, {'relevance': 0.0059563466347754, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.005647333338856697, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0028495003934949636, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.0027625008951872587, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4322154, 'end': 4348700}, 'sentences_idx_start': 600, 'sentences_idx_end': 604}, {'text': "The suggestion you're making there is it sounds like what you're saying that these things you call them psychotenologies, which I really like. Like language, like certain aspects of self modeling. They are a kind of scaffolding or like a ladder that you then kind of gets kicked away once you reach a certain kind of edge of criticality, like where the performance becomes I don't know what you're performing at such a level that you just don't need those scaffolding. Yeah.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03807730972766876, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.032325517386198044, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.030359266325831413, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.026764357462525368, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.02207382768392563, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.015078709460794926, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.012348951771855354, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.011143824085593224, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.006509528495371342, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.00622863182798028, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4349360, 'end': 4382664}, 'sentences_idx_start': 605, 'sentences_idx_end': 608}, {'text': "Or the self regulatory mechanisms that we harness when we're not in flow are linguistic or agentic in essence. And you don't need that when you're at this edge of criticality. And I only postulate that because I'm only thinking, how deep does that go? Because I know, obviously the active inference framework is trying to tackle in some ways the hard problem as well.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6986315846443176, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.05736469849944115, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.027517259120941162, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.002642180537804961, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.0022158001083880663, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.0011647541541606188, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0009539948077872396, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0009378858958370984, 'label': 'Education>EducationalAssessment'}, {'relevance': 0.0008548545301891863, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>RoleplayingGames'}, {'relevance': 0.0006869897479191422, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4382782, 'end': 4416868}, 'sentences_idx_start': 609, 'sentences_idx_end': 612}, {'text': "And there are some flotations of the idea, at least within the flow community, about the kind of I don't want to say elimination, but the moderation, the modulation of qualia under flow states. So could we also consider that to be a construct which happens when we're not necessarily optimally producing prediction error, a couple of things. So I'm certainly not the person to stop talking about consciousness, so I won't.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.42511481046676636, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.035048216581344604, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.01595386490225792, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0060152397491037846, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005195414647459984, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0025064845103770494, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.002120601711794734, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.001185620785690844, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0010678305989131331, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0008732453570701182, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4417034, 'end': 4451348}, 'sentences_idx_start': 613, 'sentences_idx_end': 615}, {'text': "But some of the readings that I mentioned in the lecture might be interesting for you on this topic. So if we're talking about certain structures that seem very pervasive in our phenomenology and how those structures can sometimes kind of dissolve away and how that might be accounted for under an active inference framework, there's some really interesting work on psychedelics by George Dean and some of George Dean's co conspirators.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9455326795578003, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.7152224183082581, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.18520264327526093, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.04060114175081253, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.02273116260766983, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.016457218676805496, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.016028959304094315, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.012056670151650906, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0037370515055954456, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.003153262659907341, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4451544, 'end': 4486628}, 'sentences_idx_start': 616, 'sentences_idx_end': 617}, {'text': "I know Mark and Sam Wilkinson worked on a paper with George so George Dean's done some work on kind of ego dissolution and certain kinds of experiences related to selfhood, kind of and I kind of don't want to overstep the mark, but I think they fall generally under this kind of rebus model of psychedelic efficacy. So I don't know if people are familiar with this, but this kind of finds natural articulation through predictive processing and hierarchical self modeling and that kind of stuff.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6922673583030701, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.2267453819513321, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.06537801027297974, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.06220974773168564, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.011766486801207066, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.009558090008795261, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.005877902265638113, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0021976837888360023, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.0015090067172423005, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0014677284052595496, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4486724, 'end': 4517200}, 'sentences_idx_start': 618, 'sentences_idx_end': 619}, {'text': "I also wanted to really quickly flag on this topic. I'll find the paper and I'll put it up on the coder because I don't think I'll be able to find it quickly enough now. But there was a paper that came out very recently that showed the efficacy of internal self talk on sports performance.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9500437378883362, 'label': 'Sports'}, {'relevance': 0.5504125952720642, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise>ParticipantSports'}, {'relevance': 0.2096322625875473, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.09193653613328934, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>SportingEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.057393673807382584, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.04743397235870361, 'label': 'Sports>CollegeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.012206441722810268, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise>RunningAndJogging'}, {'relevance': 0.010423127561807632, 'label': 'Sports>Bodybuilding'}, {'relevance': 0.00838435348123312, 'label': 'Sports>FantasySports'}, {'relevance': 0.006046762689948082, 'label': 'Sports>SportsEquipment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4517270, 'end': 4535400}, 'sentences_idx_start': 620, 'sentences_idx_end': 622}, {'text': "They did an experiment with cyclists and they found that when cyclists were allowed to engage in kind of constant self talk with them, like an inner monologue in their head, their performance at cycling was measurably boosted, which I thought was really interesting and kind of relevant here. But it's interesting because it sounds like it might prima facia be in tension with what we were saying about flow states as well. Right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9695370197296143, 'label': 'Sports>Cycling'}, {'relevance': 0.29307886958122253, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.11618320643901825, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>ExerciseAndFitnessVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.019011832773685455, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise>RunningAndJogging'}, {'relevance': 0.008422334678471088, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.008176049217581749, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.004393669310957193, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}, {'relevance': 0.0035072527825832367, 'label': 'Sports>DisabledSports'}, {'relevance': 0.0035001037176698446, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0024446831084787846, 'label': 'Sports>Walking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4537660, 'end': 4567924}, 'sentences_idx_start': 623, 'sentences_idx_end': 625}, {'text': "So if the real edge of performance is a place where these structures of phenomenology bleed away, it kind of calls into question, like, to what extent are these psychotechnologies effective and in what way are they effective? There's just a whole kind of universe of really interesting questions there. So, if I may, self food, indirectly will be the central topic of the last two sessions.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6099782586097717, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.363120436668396, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>MagicAndIllusion'}, {'relevance': 0.1501176357269287, 'label': 'FineArt>Theater'}, {'relevance': 0.07970701903104782, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.045408423990011215, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.020166797563433647, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.008831299841403961, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.007935970090329647, 'label': 'Sports>ExtremeSports'}, {'relevance': 0.007243090774863958, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.006756275426596403, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>ComedyEvents'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4567962, 'end': 4594620}, 'sentences_idx_start': 626, 'sentences_idx_end': 628}, {'text': 'My position about it is that self food, in a sense, we use all of the time, is a quite high level construct that emerges from the ability we have to compare our activity to a socially embedded model of our activity. So that is something that is quite specific to humans because of their linguistic ability and or because of their tendency to what Thomaslo calls shared intentionality. So the ability to collectively define an.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9850724339485168, 'label': 'Food&Drink'}, {'relevance': 0.43043386936187744, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>FoodIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.3289872109889984, 'label': 'Food&Drink>FoodMovements'}, {'relevance': 0.1695476919412613, 'label': 'Food&Drink>HealthyCookingAndEating'}, {'relevance': 0.15221627056598663, 'label': 'Food&Drink>Cooking'}, {'relevance': 0.02662142552435398, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Nutrition'}, {'relevance': 0.02239537611603737, 'label': 'Food&Drink>DiningOut'}, {'relevance': 0.009891010820865631, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Cookbooks'}, {'relevance': 0.008739082142710686, 'label': 'Food&Drink>WorldCuisines'}, {'relevance': 0.006993611343204975, 'label': 'Food&Drink>VegetarianDiets'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4595520, 'end': 4628970}, 'sentences_idx_start': 629, 'sentences_idx_end': 631}, {'text': "So basically, this is something that enables a very deep, very profound and robust transmission of cultural knowledge and transmission of norms. This is what enables the construction of norms. But it's quite heavy cognitively and it is predictable that if you're busy comparing what you do to what an idealized version of yourself is doing, you're going to invest less creative energy in actually doing the thing that you would if you just did a thing.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.14443360269069672, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.0739792138338089, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Men'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.041218020021915436, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingTeens'}, {'relevance': 0.033571112900972366, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingChildrenAged4-11'}, {'relevance': 0.011093269102275372, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.011035104282200336, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Crime'}, {'relevance': 0.007293146103620529, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.007222396787256002, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.004236143082380295, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships'}, {'relevance': 0.0027755943592637777, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4631180, 'end': 4662784}, 'sentences_idx_start': 632, 'sentences_idx_end': 634}, {'text': "So I'd say you have a pretty direct entailment of this flow thing from this model. Yeah. Yes. This is my conclusion. Sorry. So we've run almost 30 minutes over time and I know Mark's had to go and I'm going to have to go very I think I pretty much have to go. So I just wondered if anybody has any final kind of quick questions or comments, maybe we can move towards wrapping it up.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.07297325134277344, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}, {'relevance': 0.0238995011895895, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>DataStorageAndWarehousing'}, {'relevance': 0.0075813839212059975, 'label': 'PersonalFinance>FinancialPlanning'}, {'relevance': 0.005733173806220293, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Sales'}, {'relevance': 0.00502717075869441, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>Logistics'}, {'relevance': 0.0033899731934070587, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.003334427485242486, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0021716735791414976, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0015734514454379678, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0013619958190247416, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessBanking&Finance>MergersAndAcquisitions'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4662982, 'end': 4695710}, 'sentences_idx_start': 635, 'sentences_idx_end': 641}, {'text': "I'll make a few comments, but Ben, you're welcome to leave and other people welcome to stay if they would like. Thank you for well, first, just on a logistical note, there was a little bit of lag.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.048675790429115295, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}, {'relevance': 0.017565442249178886, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.012710806913673878, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Camping'}, {'relevance': 0.002951054833829403, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Cruises'}, {'relevance': 0.002577931620180607, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>FamilyTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0023663919419050217, 'label': 'RealEstate>OfficeProperty'}, {'relevance': 0.002092387294396758, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>Bed&Breakfasts'}, {'relevance': 0.001899010268971324, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>BusinessTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.0018099293811246753, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>DayTrips'}, {'relevance': 0.0016766454791650176, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AirTravel'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4698560, 'end': 4717856}, 'sentences_idx_start': 642, 'sentences_idx_end': 643}, {'text': "So I'll encourage everyone who's listening, as well as who's participating, that we eventually plan to, as with all of our live streams, develop a transcript which will be curated and published, and eventually not so far away in the future, that'll be enabled with speech modeling to generate podcast quality audio. So the future will be smooth, we promise. But a few really interesting pieces that I picked out while I was embodying and listening.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.3098090589046478, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.10642414540052414, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>VideoProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.07777842879295349, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.04741576686501503, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>AudioProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.03418942540884018, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>TalkRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.020780527964234352, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>VideoSoftware'}, {'relevance': 0.0111188143491745, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>TalkRadio>EducationalRadio'}, {'relevance': 0.01099658478051424, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>DigitalAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.010216188617050648, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.009016123600304127, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>Screenwriting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4717968, 'end': 4748040}, 'sentences_idx_start': 644, 'sentences_idx_end': 646}, {'text': "So, Regina, you opened the discussion with surprise and creativity, and indeed, it sounds like it's going to be attention. How can a framework whose imperative is bounded surprise as opposed to, say, maximized reward? How can a framework whose imperative is surprise, minimization and bounding be used to generate novelty? And I felt like people provided a lot of really cool answers. And one other thing it reminds me of is Doug Hofstadter's notion of spectishnish.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.023556213825941086, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.02228974923491478, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.02100875787436962, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.015133265405893326, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}, {'relevance': 0.011690462939441204, 'label': 'Shopping>SalesAndPromotions'}, {'relevance': 0.009863329119980335, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0077689532190561295, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>EducationalVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.006256878841668367, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.006246845703572035, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.00456390343606472, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4749420, 'end': 4781884}, 'sentences_idx_start': 647, 'sentences_idx_end': 651}, {'text': "I don't know, how do you pronounce it, but sphexishness, and it's the specs wasp. And so he says, well, forget this whole creativity thing, because when we talk about creativity, it's like some sort of pantheon, like divine status. The muses have to be called in. And so then, oh, that's not real creativity, and this isn't real creativity. So instead, he says, well, let's just focus on what would be the opposite.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.017059799283742905, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.011474577710032463, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.007102340925484896, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005521029699593782, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.005375175271183252, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.0039673433639109135, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.003923824056982994, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.003031114349141717, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0018274984322488308, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}, {'relevance': 0.0017401824006810784, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4781952, 'end': 4808108}, 'sentences_idx_start': 652, 'sentences_idx_end': 656}, {'text': "And that would be the rote procedural following, even when there's an opportunity for what we would call creativity. And then there's a continuum. So why does somebody paint that painting? Well, why didn't they invent a new genre? Well, why didn't they invent a new media? And so all activity is existing within this continuum of creativeness, which has many features such as generativity and productivity, but also novelty, but abounded novelty.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9990014433860779, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.9652947187423706, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.7362418174743652, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.34034883975982666, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>Painting'}, {'relevance': 0.20070776343345642, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.180518239736557, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.05930468067526817, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts'}, {'relevance': 0.053243283182382584, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.02005361206829548, 'label': 'FineArt>FineArtPhotography'}, {'relevance': 0.018496733158826828, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4808284, 'end': 4839204}, 'sentences_idx_start': 657, 'sentences_idx_end': 662}, {'text': "It's not creative to knock the chessboard pieces off in a way that there might be an elegant chess move who only somebody in a certain cognitive setting could detect the aesthetics of. But I think that was awesome. And then the second piece that really was powerful was what mark's train.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.45413610339164734, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.25432077050209045, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0537227988243103, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.046648744493722916, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.045884471386671066, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.04445747286081314, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>PuzzleVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.04154752939939499, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.02578180469572544, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.023009108379483223, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles'}, {'relevance': 0.017387457191944122, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>GamesAndPuzzles>BoardGamesAndPuzzles'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4839252, 'end': 4862370}, 'sentences_idx_start': 663, 'sentences_idx_end': 665}, {'text': "I guess the trains don't run on time where Mark is, but that's okay, because he was able to, rather than treat that as an undigestible surprise, that was able to be basically cognitively metabolized into an opportunity for friendship through language as a social medium. And then he connected that to cognitive flexibility and coaching. And then I thought about self talk and our inner monologue inner voice.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7068285942077637, 'label': 'Education>LanguageLearning'}, {'relevance': 0.10577573627233505, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.05025329068303108, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.03269294276833534, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.027548551559448242, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.012905655428767204, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.012810270301997662, 'label': 'Education>HomeworkAndStudy'}, {'relevance': 0.01083068735897541, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Parenting>ParentingBabiesAndToddlers'}, {'relevance': 0.010671796277165413, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.009258626028895378, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MediaIndustry'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4862900, 'end': 4894140}, 'sentences_idx_start': 666, 'sentences_idx_end': 668}, {'text': "And then Darius, that was very provocative, that we aren't having self talk, potentially not even having a self in the flow, manifold experience of the self or the self talk, or again, potentially even the total actual self as a technology.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9635870456695557, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.6526818871498108, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.10717086493968964, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.07149209082126617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.017017504200339317, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.008493771776556969, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.005890735890716314, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MediaIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.005866263993084431, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.004770411178469658, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>InformationServicesIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.004048181232064962, 'label': 'PopCulture'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4894800, 'end': 4913730}, 'sentences_idx_start': 669, 'sentences_idx_end': 669}, {'text': "And so then healthy self talk would guide us to the flow and be kind of like a self limiting technology because it would be used in order to not be needed to be used, which is kind of how we would hope adaptive technologies would be versus a maladaptive technology would be something that entrenches its own utilization potentially at the expense of the functionality. Kind of like doom scrolling status. But that's internal rumination. And those are the kinds of things that people have simulated in active inference.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8960974812507629, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.7718616724014282, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.17575283348560333, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.062332529574632645, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.04583767428994179, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.045280326157808304, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.021487973630428314, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.010459206998348236, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.009293043054640293, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}, {'relevance': 0.008375663310289383, 'label': 'Careers>RemoteWorking'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4914120, 'end': 4955360}, 'sentences_idx_start': 670, 'sentences_idx_end': 673}, {'text': "So those were some really cool pieces. That was a great discussion. Could I just add something on the topic of creativity that I should have said earlier as well? Because I think it's really relevant to Regina's question and just the topic of creative and novel behaviors in general under active inference.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.46598947048187256, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.3270067274570465, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.0714876726269722, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.060491450130939484, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.02620268240571022, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.022422952577471733, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.01973382569849491, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}, {'relevance': 0.013546918518841267, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.013273430988192558, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>EntertainmentIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.009853033348917961, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4955700, 'end': 4975024}, 'sentences_idx_start': 674, 'sentences_idx_end': 677}, {'text': "I think that whenever we talk about especially artistic creativity, there's a tendency, even for people who are kind of very well burrowed into active inference and activism and these kinds of frameworks from cognitive science, I think there's a tendency to think of creativity as still like it's almost like the last bastion of internal cognitiveist thinking. We think creativity is something that happens in here and bursts outwards. And so how does that happen with this kind of whatever cognitive architecture we're positing?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9927592277526855, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.8367568850517273, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.7810531258583069, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.6495920419692993, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.10068535059690475, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.04252344369888306, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.02716090902686119, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.011850903742015362, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts'}, {'relevance': 0.009995453990995884, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0074229491874575615, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>Painting'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4975072, 'end': 5010300}, 'sentences_idx_start': 678, 'sentences_idx_end': 680}, {'text': "But there's really very cool work by I have to give a shout out to Mike Wheeler, who has written some papers on the extended mind and creativity. And one thing that's not really come up very much that I didn't get time to talk about in the lecture is this really nice natural marriage between the extended mind and active inference, something that Andy Clark has been working on. And I know he's going to be doing a lot more work on it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.15150226652622223, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.07564184814691544, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.02081899158656597, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.013693044893443584, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.012833942659199238, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.01060336921364069, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.009624571539461613, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.009120864793658257, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.006582499016076326, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004371325951069593, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5010460, 'end': 5035016}, 'sentences_idx_start': 681, 'sentences_idx_end': 683}, {'text': "But the claim Wheeler makes and some others I think Joanna Zelenska has written a little bit about this as well, is the fact that creativity itself is just as subject to kind of material, the sculpting effects of material environments and sociocultural environments as everything else is. So creativity is not this kind of romantic with a capital R kind of internal process that kind of bursts forth, but creative thinking is just as much extended and embedded as everything else. And there's some really great examples in Mike Wheeler's essay.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9195833802223206, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.49169453978538513, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.2288450002670288, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.2024831920862198, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.16544456779956818, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.06105901673436165, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts'}, {'relevance': 0.05719686672091484, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.01661815121769905, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.013212515972554684, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.008994689211249352, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5035038, 'end': 5073940}, 'sentences_idx_start': 684, 'sentences_idx_end': 686}, {'text': "I don't know, is anybody familiar with the band Alt J? They're a British band. They were kind of really big a few years ago. They won the Mercury Music Award because they have a super original sound. So AltJ have this really quiet tinkling. Yeah, they are a great band. They're one of my favorites. And they have this really quiet tinky sound that everybody kind of assumed was just the result of some kind of internal genius on the part of the band.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6427290439605713, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Inspirational/NewAgeMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.2180318981409073, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>SoftRock'}, {'relevance': 0.03585078567266464, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>AlternativeRock'}, {'relevance': 0.025800546631217003, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.015622450038790703, 'label': "MusicAndAudio>Children'sMusic"}, {'relevance': 0.01341188419610262, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>DanceAndElectronicMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.01162012293934822, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>HardRock'}, {'relevance': 0.01015195157378912, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>AlternativeMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.009875266812741756, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>AdultContemporaryMusic>SoftACMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.007913300767540932, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Songwriters/Folk'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5074280, 'end': 5101340}, 'sentences_idx_start': 687, 'sentences_idx_end': 694}, {'text': "And as it turns out, AltJ, originally they tried to rehearse as an indie rock band, but they were confined to rehearsing in an apartment block, and they kept getting noise complaints. And so they ended up developing this quiet tinkly sound because it was the only sound they could rehearse that wouldn't get them kicked out of their apartment.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5557017922401428, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Inspirational/NewAgeMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.43822264671325684, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>HardRock'}, {'relevance': 0.298668771982193, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.2559494376182556, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>AlternativeRock'}, {'relevance': 0.07439020276069641, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>SoftRock'}, {'relevance': 0.025752129033207893, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>DanceAndElectronicMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.021819740533828735, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>ClassicRock'}, {'relevance': 0.011958061717450619, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>AlternativeMusic'}, {'relevance': 0.0038384960498660803, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio'}, {'relevance': 0.0029183251317590475, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>RockMusic>Album-orientedRock'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5101840, 'end': 5123200}, 'sentences_idx_start': 695, 'sentences_idx_end': 696}, {'text': "And I think this is a really beautiful example of how even the most creative processes that seem, on the face of it, really creative, are in fact just a subject to these external kind of this kind of agent environment system that underpins the whole framework. So that's something that's going to apply to absolutely everything. Awesome. And just the last question, people are welcome to drop off the next section that we're heading into.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6357824802398682, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.43936729431152344, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.15941815078258514, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.14652064442634583, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0372873954474926, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.010524392127990723, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.009508032351732254, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.007427680306136608, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.007252189796417952, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.005489743314683437, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessOperations'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5123360, 'end': 5152896}, 'sentences_idx_start': 697, 'sentences_idx_end': 700}, {'text': "I'll be doing the lecture that's going to be in August, and it's going to be on collective behavior. So what would people like to learn or focus on about collective behavior? Anyone who hasn't spoken or it can just be a thought question, but I haven't prepared the slides at all, so I'm happy to take suggestions. Yeah, Darius and then anyone else?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.09515883028507233, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.002406234387308359, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.0023425929248332977, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0018883150769397616, 'label': 'Education>OnlineEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0011185414623469114, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.0008674981072545052, 'label': 'PopCulture'}, {'relevance': 0.0007579419761896133, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>WebConferencing'}, {'relevance': 0.0007356278947554529, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>Concerts&MusicEvents'}, {'relevance': 0.0007205897709354758, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>FanConventions'}, {'relevance': 0.0006752884946763515, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>Non-ProfitOrganizations'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5152998, 'end': 5194590}, 'sentences_idx_start': 701, 'sentences_idx_end': 704}, {'text': "I think what might be interesting is if we're saying that these systems are all in the business of reducing prediction error, of self evidencing. Why do we see a diversity why do we see a diversity of social cultures, of norms, of standards at a global scale? Why do we not just see some homogeneous way to reduce picture there, which would manifest as the kind of singular culture which is in the kind of business of self evidencing? That just kind of popped in my mind. Cool.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.6975120306015015, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.1320762038230896, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.13013723492622375, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.04267507046461105, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.01685919053852558, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.014305938966572285, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.0024641319178044796, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.001613499829545617, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0009645310929045081, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.0006548292003571987, 'label': 'Science>Environment'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5194960, 'end': 5236810}, 'sentences_idx_start': 705, 'sentences_idx_end': 709}, {'text': "Anyone else want to give a thought on collective behavior or on any other aspect? Otherwise it's been great. I'd like to make a comment of creativity, but does anyone like at the moment, if you want to make a comment on the next session, I want to put that. Okay, go for it. I'd say that to complement what Ben said, that creativity is intrinsically very hard to model because by definition, creativity is something that brings about something new, let us say.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.03892159461975098, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}, {'relevance': 0.03853527456521988, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.02243875153362751, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.010910357348620892, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction'}, {'relevance': 0.00797118991613388, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004827865865081549, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004268359858542681, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>SocialNetworking'}, {'relevance': 0.003008705098181963, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.002462847623974085, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.001810987712815404, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>OutdoorActivities'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5241920, 'end': 5280890}, 'sentences_idx_start': 710, 'sentences_idx_end': 714}, {'text': "And the mathematics we have to describe physics and life, they are not very good at new things. Because the most basic tool you have, the basic way to represent a system that literally everyone uses, is a stead space, which is the least of all possibilities of a system. If you say something is creative, you're likely to think that it means it can bring about new possibilities. And this intuition, it conflicts directly with the very basic use of math. Describe it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.972788393497467, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.6518852710723877, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.03631843253970146, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.02998412773013115, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.010451208800077438, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.005483516491949558, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>TechnologyIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.0024721845984458923, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0024238533806055784, 'label': 'Science>Chemistry'}, {'relevance': 0.002269526943564415, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0019328549969941378, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5281340, 'end': 5317924}, 'sentences_idx_start': 715, 'sentences_idx_end': 719}, {'text': "So it is basically the same issues I was referring to earlier when I talked about the comparison between active inference and an activist. So let's say activity biology inspired model of cognition, and a core concept historically in those circles is autopoiesis. So the ability of the living to self create, literally, this is Greek for self creation. And you had a lot of drift and conceptualization and ambiguities that were resolved or not resolved and led to the crisis of framework, blah, blah, blah.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.43201643228530884, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.191327765583992, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PoliticalEvent'}, {'relevance': 0.10775133967399597, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.10355152189731598, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics>PoliticalIssues'}, {'relevance': 0.032344505190849304, 'label': 'NewsAndPolitics>Politics'}, {'relevance': 0.016370054334402084, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.007576832082122564, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0059018549509346485, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>ExecutiveLeadership&Management'}, {'relevance': 0.0031906110234558582, 'label': 'Education>AdultEducation'}, {'relevance': 0.0031456623692065477, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5318042, 'end': 5353096}, 'sentences_idx_start': 720, 'sentences_idx_end': 723}, {'text': "But today we talk of autonomy rather than autopoiesis. And we define autonomy as the property for a system of constraints over the activity of a system to reproduce themselves. And because we're talking constraints, just the ability to influence causality outcomes, there is no really a prior that dynamics in this space would be conservative. So we have a possibility for constraints to bring about new things and reconfigure themselves. And the notion of Hydrancy ADUs is based on that.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8180062174797058, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.04356936365365982, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.03990289196372032, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.008376507088541985, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>CloudComputing'}, {'relevance': 0.006306351162493229, 'label': 'Home&Garden>SmartHome'}, {'relevance': 0.0029130824841558933, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>OperatingSystems'}, {'relevance': 0.0025119795463979244, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0012385312002152205, 'label': 'Science>Physics'}, {'relevance': 0.001122480258345604, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoTechnology'}, {'relevance': 0.0009192198631353676, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5353208, 'end': 5389050}, 'sentences_idx_start': 724, 'sentences_idx_end': 728}, {'text': "It's the ability to, let's say, reconfigure constraints in your environment, and so is the notion of creativity, which would be likely a very close proxy to that. But it's something that we do not know how to present. And most of the mathematics that exist are structurally enabled, represent. And so, yeah, that's a big one. So true. Michael, good to be here. Sorry I was late.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7579607963562012, 'label': 'FineArt>Design'}, {'relevance': 0.03895430266857147, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.021387318149209023, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.015924375504255295, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.01235386822372675, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ArtsAndCrafts>DrawingAndSketching'}, {'relevance': 0.004185418598353863, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.00401823315769434, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Industries>MechanicalAndIndustrialEngineeringIndustry'}, {'relevance': 0.00336844171397388, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications'}, {'relevance': 0.0033434247598052025, 'label': 'Home&Garden>Landscaping'}, {'relevance': 0.0033150147646665573, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5389500, 'end': 5428580}, 'sentences_idx_start': 729, 'sentences_idx_end': 735}, {'text': 'What comes to mind for me at the know, I mentioned units of collective, like, what is it, a we? Is it a we a pair? What are the units of we. And any thoughts or insights about that? The stages of the emergence of formation into a collective from a me to a we, for example, or god, I had one was on the tip of my tongue, and it just escaped me. Oh.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.02469056472182274, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.006153922528028488, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'